"ref_id":"turn1search8","snippet":"Video ... Space Fortress © 1981 Century Electronics.","title":"Space Fortress (CVS) - MAME machine","url":"https://adb.arcadeitalia.net/dettaglio_mame.php?game_name=spacefrt"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"allincolorforaquarter.blogspot.com","ref_id":"turn1search9","snippet":"Other early titles included Space Fortress (a color version of Asteroids), Dazzler (a maze/climbing game in which the player avoided pursuing vultures while feeding bananas","title":"The Golden Age Arcade Historian: Century Electronics/CVS","url":"https://allincolorforaquarter.blogspot.com/2014/01/century-electronicscvs.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"gamesdb.launchbox-app.com","ref_id":"turn1search10","snippet":"Century Electronics also released an arcade title in 1981 as Space Fortress, but it is unrelated to Zaccaria's Star Castle clone. ... Video ... Image:","title":"Star Castle - LaunchBox Games Database","url":"https://gamesdb.launchbox-app.com/games/details/12392-star-castle"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.arcade-museum.com","ref_id":"turn1search11","snippet":"/Video Games (UK) LTD | 1980 | Videogame | Shooter | | | ... Space Fortress | Century Electronics | 1981 | Videogame | Space","title":"All Amusement Machines: s | Museum of the Game","url":"https://www.arcade-museum.com/game-list/S/All"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"finances.belgium.be","ref_id":"turn1search15","snippet":"<td>(1 ou 2 joueurs); analogue à \"Space Firebird\".</td> ... <td>Space Fortress</td> <td>(Century Electronics)</td>","title":"<table id=\"e1\">","url":"https://finances.belgium.be/sites/default/files/downloads/124-repertoire-ancien-jeux-videos-20200326.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"unglueit-files.s3.amazonaws.com","ref_id":"turn1search16","snippet":"like Donkey Kong; and Space Fortress (1981), which is an Asteroids clone, but ... ary 1984, Century Electronics went into administration (it subsequently sold","title":"Arcade Britannia","url":"https://unglueit-files.s3.amazonaws.com/ebf/9b296840c4804664b82c3a50921d7e49.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"onitama.tv","ref_id":"turn1search17","snippet":"177, November 15, 1981 ... Three gameplay screenshots accompany an illustration of a spacecraft and space battle. ... (JLC) of Tokyo, that JLC signed an","title":"Game Machine","url":"https://onitama.tv/gamemachine/pdf/19811115p.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"pub.deadnet.se","ref_id":"turn1search18","snippet":"Nintendo did ﬁnd success with a game they released in 1981. ... games, including Century Electronics’s Space Fortress and Sega’s Space Fury, and one game,","title":"THE VIDEO GAME EXPLOSION","url":"https://pub.deadnet.se/Books_and_manuals_on_various_stuff/Computers/Computer%20Science/Wolf%20-%20Video%20Game%20Explosion%20-%20A%20History%20from%20Pong%20to%20Playstation%20%28Greenwood%2C%202008%29.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"ballyalley.com","ref_id":"turn1search19","snippet":"SPACE FORTRESS ... Turn on your Bally Professional Arcade and TV set.","title":"SPACE FORTRESS 2012","url":"https://ballyalley.com/cart_manuals/pdf_manuals/Space_Fortress%20%28OCR%29.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn1search20","snippet":"List of arcade video games: S ... Space Fortress | — | 1981 | Century Electronics | |","title":"List of arcade video games: S","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_arcade_video_games%3A_S"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn1search21","snippet":"It consists of two games which can be played independently or one after the other: Space Fortress, which is a clone of the arcade video","title":"Escape from Arcturus","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Escape_from_Arcturus"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn1search22","snippet":"Zaxxon is a 1981 scrolling shooter developed and published by Sega as an arcade video game. ... The player pilots a ship through two heavily","title":"Zaxxon","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zaxxon"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"it.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn1search23","snippet":"* (EN) Space Demon - Videogame by Fortrek, su arcade-museum.com.","title":"Space Firebird","url":"https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Firebird"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn1search24","snippet":"Space Zap is a space-themed fixed shooter arcade video game developed by Game-A-Tron and licensed to Midway Manufacturing in 1980. ... An official port of","title":"Space Zap","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Zap"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"arxiv.org","ref_id":"turn1academia25","snippet":"Research in deep reinforcement learning (RL) has coalesced around improving performance on benchmarks like the Arcade Learning Environment. ... To tackle this issue, this paper","title":"Challenges of Context and Time in Reinforcement Learning: Introducing Space Fortress as a Benchmark","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.02206"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn1search26","snippet":"Super Spacefortress Macross was moderately popular in arcades; In Japan, Game Machine listed it on their October 15, 1992 issue as being the seventh most-popular","title":"Super Spacefortress Macross (video game)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Spacefortress_Macross_%28video_game%29"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.reddit.com","ref_id":"turn1reddit27","snippet":"https://www.arcade-museum.com/Videogame/end-the","title":"Unknown Bezel","url":"https://www.reddit.com/r/arcadecabinets/comments/1oed8b1"}]}}
