{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,100p' vendor/hub/lib/hub/session.js && cat vendor/hub/lib/hub/examples/arena.html\"","aggregated_output":"/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\n      },\n    };\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\n    return new Proxy(api, {\n      get: function (t, k) {\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\n      },\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\n        return true;\n      },\n      has: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data || k in t;\n      },\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\n        delete data[k];\n        return true;\n      },\n      ownKeys: function () {\n        return Object.keys(data);\n      },\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\n  function generator(a) {\n    return function () {\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n      var t = a;\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n    };\n  }\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Star Arena — AI Hub session example (shared world)</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"A minimal shared-world game for the AI Hub Session Protocol: every copy moves its own player, the host runs the stars and the scores, first to ten wins.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1b1530\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Tech demo\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"2\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"First to ten stars wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: arrows, WASD or a stick · sprint: Space or Cross · or hold a finger\">\n<style>\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #1b1530; color: #f3eef7; font: 16px system-ui, sans-serif; overflow: hidden; }\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; touch-action: none; }\n</style>\n<script>\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\n      },\n    };\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\n    return new Proxy(api, {\n      get: function (t, k) {\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\n      },\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\n        return true;\n      },\n      has: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data || k in t;\n      },\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\n        delete data[k];\n        return true;\n      },\n      ownKeys: function () {\n        return Object.keys(data);\n      },\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\n  function generator(a) {\n    return function () {\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n      var t = a;\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n    };\n  }\n\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\n  if (hub.active) {\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\n      try {\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\n      } catch (e) {\n        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\n  var seededRandom = null;\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\n    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\n    hub.seeded = true;\n  }\n\n  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\n  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\n  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\n  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\n  var fullscreenOn = false;\n  if (hub.active && root.Element && root.document) {\n    var asks = function (on) {\n      return function () {\n        post('fullscreen', { on: on });\n        return Promise.resolve();\n      };\n    };\n    var proto = root.Element.prototype;\n    proto.requestFullscreen = proto.webkitRequestFullscreen = asks(true);\n    root.document.exitFullscreen = root.document.webkitExitFullscreen = asks(false);\n    var shown = function () {\n      return fullscreenOn ? root.document.documentElement || null : null;\n    };\n    try {\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'fullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'webkitFullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\n    } catch (e) {}\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * No hub after all: play on, with Math.random the page's own again. The\n   * empty storage stays: the game has read it already, and what it writes\n   * must never land on the player's real saves.\n   */\n  function standAlone() {\n    hub.active = false;\n    if (seededRandom && Math.random === seededRandom) Math.random = realRandom;\n    hub.seeded = false;\n  }\n\n  var origin = '*';\n  var welcomed = false;\n  var ended = false;\n  var connecting = null;\n  var goAt = null;\n  var sentReady = false;\n  var reported = false;\n  var handlers = {};\n  var pending = {};\n  var tokens = limits.burst;\n  var refilled = now();\n  var probeFn = null;\n  var lastProgress = -Infinity;\n  var nextProgress = null;\n  var progressTimer = null;\n\n  function now() {\n    return root.performance && root.performance.now ? root.performance.now() : Date.now();\n  }\n\n  function warn(text) {\n    if (root.console) root.console.warn('[AIHub] ' + text);\n  }\n\n  function own(o, k) {\n    return Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(o, k);\n  }\n\n  /** This client's own fields, which no welcome may overwrite. */\n  var KEEP = { aihub: 1, type: 1, version: 1, protocol: 1, active: 1, seeded: 1 };\n\n  /** A plain JSON copy, or undefined when it is not JSON. */\n  function json(value) {\n    try {\n      var text = JSON.stringify(value);\n      return text === undefined ? undefined : JSON.parse(text);\n    } catch (e) {\n      return undefined;\n    }\n  }\n\n  function post(type, fields) {\n    var msg = { aihub: 1, type: type };\n    for (var key in fields) if (own(fields, key)) msg[key] = fields[key];\n    try {\n      root.parent.postMessage(msg, origin);\n    } catch (e) {\n      warn('could not reach the hub: ' + e.message);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function emit(type, args) {\n    var list = handlers[type];\n    if (!list || !list.length || pending[type]) {\n      (pending[type] = pending[type] || []).push(args);\n      return;\n    }\n    for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\n      try {\n        list[i].apply(null, args);\n      } catch (e) {\n        setTimeout(function () {\n          throw e;\n        });\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  function onMessage(event) {\n    if (event.source !== root.parent) return;\n    var m = event.data;\n    if (!m || m.aihub !== 1 || typeof m.type !== 'string') return;\n    if (m.type === 'welcome') {\n      if (welcomed) return;\n      welcomed = true;\n      origin = event.origin && event.origin !== 'null' ? event.origin : '*';\n      // Every field the hub sends is kept, so a newer hub can add one without a newer client.\n      for (var key in m) {\n        if (!own(m, key) || KEEP[key] || typeof hub[key] === 'function') continue;\n        hub[key] = m[key];\n      }\n      hub.players = (m.players || []).slice();\n      hub.seed = m.seed >>> 0;\n      hub.isHost = m.me === m.host;\n      hub.splash = m.splash === true;\n      if (m.limits) {\n        for (var l in limits) if (own(limits, l) && Number(m.limits[l]) > 0) limits[l] = Number(m.limits[l]);\n        tokens = limits.burst;\n      }\n      if (connecting) connecting.resolve(info());\n      return;\n    }\n    if (m.type === 'fullscreen') {\n      fullscreenOn = m.on === true;\n      try {\n        root.document.dispatchEvent(new root.Event('fullscreenchange'));\n      } catch (e) {}\n      return;\n    }\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return;\n    if (m.type === 'start') {\n      goAt = now() + Number(m.in || 0);\n      emit('start', [{ in: Number(m.in || 0) }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'message') {\n      emit('message', [m.data, m.from]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'leave') {\n      hub.players = hub.players.filter(function (p) {\n        return p.id !== m.id;\n      });\n      emit('leave', [{ id: m.id, reason: m.reason }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'time-up') {\n      emit('time-up', [{ graceMs: m.graceMs }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'end') {\n      ended = true;\n      if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\n      emit('end', [{ reason: m.reason, standings: m.standings || null }]);\n    } else {\n      // An event this client has never heard of: hand it on as it came.\n      var detail = {};\n      for (var k in m) if (own(m, k) && k !== 'aihub' && k !== 'type') detail[k] = m[k];\n      emit(m.type, [detail]);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function info() {\n    var out = {};\n    for (var key in hub) if (own(hub, key) && typeof hub[key] !== 'function' && !KEEP[key]) out[key] = hub[key];\n    out.players = hub.players.slice();\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  /** Join the session. Resolves with the round's info, or null when there is no hub: play normally. */\n  hub.connect = function (opts) {\n    if (connecting) return connecting.promise;\n    var done;\n    var promise = new Promise(function (resolve) {\n      done = resolve;\n    });\n    connecting = { promise: promise, resolve: done };\n    if (!hub.active) {\n      done(null);\n      return promise;\n    }\n    opts = opts || {};\n    root.addEventListener('message', onMessage);\n    var started = now();\n    var hello = function () {\n      if (welcomed) return;\n      if (now() - started > HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS) {\n        standAlone();\n        warn('no hub answered; playing normally');\n        done(null);\n        return;\n      }\n      post('hello', { v: 1, client: VERSION, mode: opts.mode || null, seats: opts.seats || null, card: opts.card === true });\n      setTimeout(hello, HELLO_EVERY_MS);\n    };\n    hello();\n    return promise;\n  };\n\n  /** Everything is loaded: at once when info.splash, otherwise from the player's ready gesture. */\n  hub.ready = function () {\n    if (!welcomed || sentReady || ended) return;\n    sentReady = true;\n    post('ready', {});\n  };\n\n  /** On the game's own card (connect({ card: true })): this player is 'ready', or asks for 'more' time (again takes it back). */\n  hub.answer = function (what) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || goAt !== null) return;\n    if (what !== 'ready' && what !== 'more') return warn('answer is ready or more');\n    post('answer', { answer: what });\n  };\n\n  hub.on = function (type, fn) {\n    (handlers[type] = handlers[type] || []).push(fn);\n    if (pending[type] && !pending[type].flushing) {\n      pending[type].flushing = true;\n      setTimeout(function () {\n        var queued = pending[type];\n        delete pending[type];\n        for (var i = 0; i < queued.length; i++) emit(type, queued[i]);\n      });\n    }\n    return function () {\n      var list = handlers[type] || [];\n      var at = list.indexOf(fn);\n      if (at !== -1) list.splice(at, 1);\n    };\n  };\n\n  /** Send JSON data to every other player, or to one with {to: id}. {reliable: false} may drop or reorder. */\n  hub.send = function (data, opts) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return false;\n    opts = opts || {};\n    var text;\n    try {\n      text = JSON.stringify(data);\n    } catch (e) {\n      warn('send: data is not JSON');\n      return false;\n    }\n    if (text === undefined) return false;\n    if (text.length > limits.maxBytes) {\n      warn('send: message over ' + limits.maxBytes + ' bytes dropped');\n      return false;\n    }\n    var t = now();\n    tokens = Math.min(limits.burst, tokens + ((t - refilled) / 1000) * limits.ratePerS);\n    refilled = t;\n    if (tokens < 1) {\n      warn('send: over ' + limits.ratePerS + ' messages a second, dropped');\n      return false;\n    }\n    tokens -= 1;\n    var fields = { data: JSON.parse(text), reliable: opts.reliable !== false };\n    if (opts.to !== undefined && opts.to !== null) fields.to = opts.to;\n    post('send', fields);\n    return true;\n  };\n\n  /** Milliseconds since the synchronized start: negative during the countdown, -Infinity before start. */\n  hub.time = function () {\n    return goAt === null ? -Infinity : now() - goAt;\n  };\n\n  /** A seeded random number generator (0 ≤ n < 1), the same sequence on every device for the same label. */\n  hub.rng = function (label) {\n    var h = 2166136261;\n    var s = String(label === undefined ? '' : label);\n    for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n      h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\n      h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\n    }\n    return generator((hub.seed ^ h) >>> 0);\n  };\n\n  /** A number the hub can rank: finite, given as a number or as text. Not null, '' or true, which JSON or Number would make 0. */\n  function finite(v) {\n    return (typeof v === 'number' || (typeof v === 'string' && v.trim() !== '')) && isFinite(v);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * The whole outcome as plain JSON, field by field: the hub checks and trims\n   * it, so new optional fields need no new client. A field that is not JSON\n   * (a cycle, a BigInt) is left out, not the whole outcome.\n   */\n  function outcomeOf(outcome) {\n    if (!outcome || typeof outcome !== 'object' || Array.isArray(outcome)) {\n      warn('the outcome is not a plain object');\n      return null;\n    }\n    var copy = {};\n    for (var key in outcome) {\n      if (!own(outcome, key)) continue;\n      var value = json(outcome[key]);\n      if (value !== undefined) copy[key] = value;\n      else if (outcome[key] !== undefined) warn('the outcome\\'s ' + key + ' is not JSON: left out');\n    }\n    return copy;\n  }\n\n  /** Race and side by side: report your own outcome once, {time: ms} (lower wins) or {score: n} (higher wins), with optional stats and awards. */\n  hub.result = function (outcome) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\n    var fields = outcomeOf(outcome);\n    if (!fields) return;\n    var given = outcome || {};\n    delete fields.time;\n    delete fields.score;\n    if (finite(given.time)) fields.time = Number(given.time);\n    if (finite(given.score)) fields.score = Number(given.score);\n    if (!own(fields, 'time') && !own(fields, 'score')) return warn('result needs a finite time or score');\n    reported = true;\n    if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\n    post('result', fields);\n  };\n\n  /** Versus and co-op: the host reports the standings once, best first, ties grouped: [[2], [0, 3], [1]]. */\n  hub.finish = function (outcome) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\n    if (!hub.isHost) return warn('finish is for the host only');\n    var fields = outcomeOf(outcome);\n    if (!fields) return;\n    if (!Array.isArray(fields.standings)) return warn('finish needs standings');\n    reported = true;\n    post('finish', fields);\n  };\n\n  function sendProgress() {\n    progressTimer = null;\n    if (!nextProgress || ended || reported) return;\n    lastProgress = now();\n    post('progress', nextProgress);\n    nextProgress = null;\n  }\n\n  /** Your standing during play, for the hub's scoreboard: {score, label}. Call it as often as you like; the hub hears it about once a second. */\n  hub.progress = function (p) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported || !p || !finite(p.score)) return;\n    nextProgress = { score: Number(p.score) };\n    if (p.label != null) nextProgress.label = String(p.label).slice(0, 24);\n    var wait = lastProgress + PROGRESS_EVERY_MS - now();\n    if (wait <= 0) sendProgress();\n    else if (!progressTimer) progressTimer = setTimeout(sendProgress, wait);\n  };\n\n  /** For the harness, in or out of a session: fn() → { scene, menu, world, input }, read with inspect(). */\n  hub.probe = function (fn) {\n    probeFn = typeof fn === 'function' ? fn : null;\n  };\n\n  hub.inspect = function () {\n    if (!probeFn) return null;\n    try {\n      return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(probeFn()));\n    } catch (e) {\n      return { error: String((e && e.message) || e) };\n    }\n  };\n\n  /** The game cannot run here (no WebGL, failed load): the hub skips it. */\n  hub.fail = function (message) {\n    if (!hub.active) return;\n    post('error', { message: String(message || 'error').slice(0, 500), fatal: true });\n  };\n\n  root.AIHub = hub;\n})(typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis);\n</script>\n</head>\n<body>\n<canvas id=\"c\" aria-label=\"Star Arena\"></canvas>\n<script>\n'use strict';\n// Star Arena: the smallest honest shared-world game, the plain form of \"Shared\n// world\" (lib/hub/README.md): the host runs the world. Every copy moves its own\n// player from its own stick, at once, and never waits for the network to do\n// it. The host's copy runs only what is shared, the star and the scores:\n//   me     each other copy → the host, ~15 a second, unreliable: where my player is\n//   s      the host → everyone, ~15 a second, unreliable: every player, its score, the star\n//   claim  a copy → the host, reliable, once a star: my player touched star n\n//   pick   the host → everyone, reliable: player id took star n\n// The host takes each player where it says it is, and a claim scores unless\n// someone else got there first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends the round.\n// The host may be a server, a copy with no player of its own (AIHub.server):\n// it runs the same host code, moves nobody and draws nothing.\n// First to TARGET stars wins.\nconst W = 800, H = 600, R = 18, SPEED = 260, TARGET = 10;\nconst canvas = document.getElementById('c');\nconst ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\nconst keys = new Set();\nlet pointer = null;\nlet audio = null;\n\naddEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n  if (e.key === 'Escape') return toggleMenu();\n  if (menu.open) return menuKey(e.key);\n  keys.add(e.key.toLowerCase());\n  gesture();\n});\naddEventListener('keyup', (e) => keys.delete(e.key.toLowerCase()));\ncanvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => { pointer = e; gesture(); });\ncanvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => { if (pointer) pointer = e; });\naddEventListener('pointerup', () => { pointer = null; });\n\nfunction beep(freq) {\n  if (!audio || muted) return;\n  const o = audio.createOscillator(), g = audio.createGain();\n  o.frequency.value = freq; g.gain.value = 0.05;\n  o.connect(g).connect(audio.destination);\n  o.start(); o.stop(audio.currentTime + 0.08);\n}\n\n// ---- the controller, in the browser's standard mapping (a PS5 DualSense:\n// Cross 0, Circle 1, Triangle 3, Create 8, Options 9, D-pad 12-15, left stick\n// axes 0 and 1). Buttons count on the frame they go down.\nconst PAD = { cross: 0, circle: 1, triangle: 3, create: 8, options: 9, up: 12, down: 13 };\nlet pad = null, padNow = [], padWas = [];\nfunction readPad() {\n  pad = navigator.getGamepads ? [...navigator.getGamepads()].find((p) => p && p.connected) || null : null;\n  padWas = padNow;\n  padNow = pad ? pad.buttons.map((b) => b.pressed) : [];\n  // Create + Options is the hub's: it opens the hub's corner bar, so Options alone opens the menu.\n  if (pressed(PAD.options) && !padNow[PAD.create]) return toggleMenu();\n  if (menu.open) {\n    if (pressed(PAD.up)) menuKey('ArrowUp');\n    if (pressed(PAD.down)) menuKey('ArrowDown');\n    if (pressed(PAD.cross)) menuKey('Enter');\n    if (pressed(PAD.circle)) toggleMenu();\n  } else if (padNow.some((b, i) => b && !padWas[i] && i !== PAD.create && i !== PAD.options)) gesture();\n}\nconst pressed = (b) => !!padNow[b] && !padWas[b];\n\n// ---- the settings menu: Esc or Options, over the running game. It never\n// pauses anything; while it is open your player simply stands still.\nlet muted = false;\nconst menu = {\n  open: false,\n  at: 0,\n  items: [\n    { label: () => `Sound: ${muted ? 'off' : 'on'}`, act: () => { muted = !muted; } },\n    { label: () => 'Back to the game', act: () => toggleMenu() },\n  ],\n};\nfunction toggleMenu() { menu.open = !menu.open; menu.at = 0; keys.clear(); }\nfunction menuKey(key) {\n  if (key === 'ArrowUp' || key === 'w') menu.at = (menu.at + menu.items.length - 1) % menu.items.length;\n  if (key === 'ArrowDown' || key === 's') menu.at = (menu.at + 1) % menu.items.length;\n  if (key === 'Enter' || key === ' ') menu.items[menu.at].act();\n}\n\n/** The local stick: keys, the first gamepad, or a held pointer. Still while the menu is open. */\nfunction stick(me) {\n  if (menu.open) return { x: 0, y: 0, sprint: false };\n  let x = 0, y = 0;\n  if (keys.has('arrowleft') || keys.has('a')) x -= 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowright') || keys.has('d')) x += 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowup') || keys.has('w')) y -= 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowdown') || keys.has('s')) y += 1;\n  if (pad) {\n    if (Math.abs(pad.axes[0]) > 0.2) x = pad.axes[0];\n    if (Math.abs(pad.axes[1]) > 0.2) y = pad.axes[1];\n    if (padNow[12]) y = -1;\n    if (padNow[13]) y = 1;\n    if (padNow[14]) x = -1;\n    if (padNow[15]) x = 1;\n  }\n  if (pointer && me) {\n    const p = toWorld(pointer);\n    const dx = p.x - me.x, dy = p.y - me.y, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy);\n    if (d > 8) { x = dx / d; y = dy / d; }\n  }\n  const sprint = keys.has(' ') || !!padNow[PAD.cross] || !!padNow[7];\n  const len = Math.hypot(x, y);\n  return len > 1 ? { x: x / len, y: y / len, sprint } : { x, y, sprint };\n}\n\nfunction toWorld(e) {\n  const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect(), s = Math.min(r.width / W, r.height / H);\n  return { x: (e.clientX - r.left - (r.width - W * s) / 2) / s, y: (e.clientY - r.top - (r.height - H * s) / 2) / s };\n}\n\n// ---- state shared by both modes\nconst game = {\n  phase: 'title',            // title | waiting | playing | over\n  players: [],               // {id, name, color, x, y, score, gone}, drawn at x, y\n  star: { x: W / 2, y: H / 2, n: 0 },   // n numbers the stars, so a claim names the one it touched\n  rng: Math.random,\n  message: '',\n  standings: null,\n};\nlet felt = { x: 0, y: 0, sprint: false };   // the local stick as last read\n\nfunction place(players) {\n  players.forEach((p, i) => {\n    const a = (i / Math.max(players.length, 1)) * Math.PI * 2;\n    p.tx = p.x = W / 2 + Math.cos(a) * 200; p.ty = p.y = H / 2 + Math.sin(a) * 180;\n  });\n}\nfunction newStar() {\n  game.star = { x: 40 + game.rng() * (W - 80), y: 40 + game.rng() * (H - 80), n: game.star.n + 1 };\n}\n\n/** Your own player, from your own stick. Every copy moves its own, every frame, host or not. */\nfunction move(p, s, dt) {\n  const speed = SPEED * (s.sprint ? 1.5 : 1);\n  p.x = Math.max(R, Math.min(W - R, p.x + s.x * speed * dt));\n  p.y = Math.max(R, Math.min(H - R, p.y + s.y * speed * dt));\n}\nconst touching = (p) => Math.hypot(p.x - game.star.x, p.y - game.star.y) < R + 12;\n\n// ---- solo: the game as it plays on its own\nfunction solo() {\n  game.players = [{ id: 0, name: 'You', color: '#f5b700', x: W / 2, y: H / 2, score: 0 }];\n  game.phase = 'title';\n  game.message = 'Star Arena — press any key or tap to play';\n}\nlet soloEnds = 0;\n\n// ---- hub mode. Every other player also has tx, ty: where it last said it is\n// (and on the host, at: when). It is drawn easing toward there; your own player\n// is drawn where you put it.\nlet hub = null;\nlet lastSent = 0;\nlet lastSnap = -Infinity;    // the newest snapshot taken, by its AIHub.time()\nlet claimed = -1;            // the star this copy claimed last: one claim a star\n\nasync function connect() {\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4] });\n  if (!info) return solo();\n  hub = info;\n  game.rng = AIHub.rng('stars');\n  game.players = info.players.map((p) => ({ ...p, x: 0, y: 0, score: 0, gone: false, at: -Infinity }));\n  place(game.players);\n  newStar();                 // the first star comes from the seed: the same on every copy\n  // The hub's card collects everyone's ready: ready up as soon as the arena is built.\n  game.phase = 'waiting';\n  game.message = 'Get ready…';\n  AIHub.ready();\n  AIHub.on('start', () => { game.phase = 'playing'; unlockAudio(); });\n  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\n    if (hub.isHost && data.t === 'me') heard(from, data);\n    if (hub.isHost && data.t === 'claim') take(from, data.n);\n    if (from === hub.host && data.t === 's') applySnapshot(data);\n    if (from === hub.host && data.t === 'pick' && data.id !== hub.me) beep(330);   // your own cheered at the claim\n  });\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (p) p.gone = true;\n    if (hub.isHost && game.phase === 'playing' && game.players.filter((q) => !q.gone).length < 2) finish();\n  });\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (hub.isHost) finish(); });\n  AIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => {\n    game.phase = 'over';\n    game.standings = standings;\n    game.message = reason === 'finished' ? 'Round over' : reason === 'sat-out' ? 'You sat this one out' : 'Round cancelled';\n  });\n}\nconst inside = (v, max) => Math.max(R, Math.min(max - R, Number(v) || 0));\n\n/** Host: a player says where it is, and there it is, unless an older report arrived late. */\nfunction heard(id, m) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (!p || !(m.at > p.at)) return;\n  p.at = m.at; p.tx = inside(m.x, W); p.ty = inside(m.y, H);\n}\n\n/** Host: player id touched star n. It scores, unless someone else got there first. */\nfunction take(id, n) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (game.phase !== 'playing' || !p || p.gone || n !== game.star.n) return;\n  p.score++;\n  newStar();\n  beep(id === hub.me ? 660 : 330);\n  AIHub.send({ t: 'pick', id, n });\n  if (p.score >= TARGET) finish();\n}\n\n/** Host: one snapshot for everyone: every player still here with its score, and the star. */\nfunction snapshot() {\n  const spot = (p) => (p.id === hub.me ? [p.x, p.y] : [p.tx, p.ty]);   // the others: where they said\n  return {\n    t: 's',\n    at: Math.round(AIHub.time()),\n    p: game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).map((p) => [p.id, ...spot(p).map(Math.round), p.score]),\n    s: [Math.round(game.star.x), Math.round(game.star.y), game.star.n],\n  };\n}\n\n/** Not the host: take the scores, the star and the other players from the snapshot, never your own player. */\nfunction applySnapshot(s) {\n  if (s.at < lastSnap) return;   // unreliable: an older one that arrived late\n  lastSnap = s.at;\n  for (const [id, x, y, score] of s.p) {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (!p) continue;\n    p.score = score;\n    if (id !== hub.me) { p.tx = x; p.ty = y; }\n  }\n  game.star = { x: s.s[0], y: s.s[1], n: s.s[2] };\n  if (s.over) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = 'Round over'; }\n}\n\n/** Host: standings by score, ties together, best first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends every copy on the same scores. */\nfunction finish() {\n  if (game.phase === 'over') return;\n  AIHub.send({ ...snapshot(), over: 1 });\n  const live = game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);\n  const standings = [];\n  for (const p of live) {\n    const last = standings[standings.length - 1];\n    if (last && last.score === p.score) last.ids.push(p.id);\n    else standings.push({ score: p.score, ids: [p.id] });\n  }\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(game.players.map((p) => [p.id, p.score]));\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: standings.map((g) => g.ids), scores });\n  game.phase = 'over';\n  game.message = 'Round over';\n}\n\nfunction unlockAudio() {\n  if (!audio) {\n    try { audio = new AudioContext(); } catch { audio = null; }\n  }\n  audio?.resume?.().catch(() => {});\n}\n\nfunction gesture() {\n  unlockAudio();\n  if (!hub && (game.phase === 'title' || game.phase === 'over')) {\n    solo();\n    game.phase = 'playing';\n    soloEnds = performance.now() + 60_000;\n  }\n}\n\n// ---- the loop: advance by elapsed time, never pause\nlet last = performance.now();\nfunction frame(now) {\n  const dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25);\n  last = now;\n  readPad();\n  const me = game.players.find((p) => p.id === (hub ? hub.me : 0));\n  felt = stick(me);\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && (!hub || AIHub.time() >= 0)) {\n    if (me) move(me, felt, dt);   // now, on every copy: your controls never wait for the network\n    if (hub) play(now, dt, me);\n    else {\n      if (touching(me)) { me.score++; newStar(); beep(660); }\n      if (now > soloEnds) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = `Time! ${me.score} stars — press to play again`; }\n    }\n  }\n  if (!hub?.server) draw(now);   // a server runs the world and needs no picture of it\n  requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\n\n/** A session frame, after your own move: the star, what this copy sends, and the others eased toward where they are. */\nfunction play(now, dt, me) {\n  if (me && touching(me)) {\n    if (hub.isHost) take(hub.me, game.star.n);\n    else if (claimed !== game.star.n) {\n      // Predict the contact: claim the star once, hide it and cheer now. The host decides the point.\n      claimed = game.star.n;\n      AIHub.send({ t: 'claim', n: claimed }, { to: hub.host });\n      beep(660);\n    }\n  }\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && now - lastSent > 66) {\n    lastSent = now;\n    if (hub.isHost) AIHub.send(snapshot(), { reliable: false });\n    else AIHub.send({ t: 'me', at: Math.round(AIHub.time()), x: Math.round(me.x), y: Math.round(me.y) }, { to: hub.host, reliable: false });\n  }\n  const k = 1 - Math.pow(0.001, dt);\n  for (const p of game.players) if (p !== me) { p.x += (p.tx - p.x) * k; p.y += (p.ty - p.y) * k; }\n}\n\nfunction draw(now) {\n  const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\n  const dpr = devicePixelRatio || 1;\n  if (canvas.width !== Math.round(r.width * dpr) || canvas.height !== Math.round(r.height * dpr)) {\n    canvas.width = Math.round(r.width * dpr); canvas.height = Math.round(r.height * dpr);\n  }\n  const s = Math.min(canvas.width / W, canvas.height / H);\n  ctx.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#120e22'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  ctx.setTransform(s, 0, 0, s, (canvas.width - W * s) / 2, (canvas.height - H * s) / 2);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#1b1530'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n\n  if (game.star.n !== claimed) {   // a star you claimed is gone here until the host's next one arrives\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#ffd34d';\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(game.star.x, game.star.y, 10 + Math.sin(now / 150) * 2, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();\n  }\n\n  ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n  for (const p of game.players) {\n    if (p.gone) continue;\n    ctx.fillStyle = p.color;\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(p.x, p.y, R, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7'; ctx.font = '14px system-ui';\n    ctx.fillText(`${p.name} ${p.score}`, p.x, p.y - R - 8);\n  }\n\n  ctx.font = '22px system-ui';\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7';\n  if (hub && game.phase === 'playing' && AIHub.time() < 0) {\n    ctx.font = 'bold 96px system-ui';\n    ctx.fillText(String(Math.ceil(-AIHub.time() / 1000)), W / 2, H / 2 + 32);\n  } else if (game.phase !== 'playing') {\n    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(0,0,0,.55)'; ctx.fillRect(0, H / 2 - 120, W, 240);\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7';\n    ctx.fillText(game.message, W / 2, H / 2 - 70);\n    const rows = game.standings\n      ? game.standings.flatMap((ids, place) => ids.map((id) => [place + 1, game.players.find((p) => p.id === id)]))\n      : game.players.map((p) => [null, p]);\n    ctx.font = '18px system-ui';\n    rows.slice(0, 4).forEach(([place, p], i) => {\n      if (!p) return;\n      ctx.fillStyle = p.color;\n      ctx.fillText(`${place ? place + '. ' : ''}${p.name}${hub && p.id === hub.me ? ' (you)' : ''} — ${p.score}`, W / 2, H / 2 - 30 + i * 28);\n    });\n  }\n  if (menu.open) drawMenu();\n}\n\nfunction drawMenu() {\n  ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(10,8,20,.82)'; ctx.fillRect(W / 2 - 170, 150, 340, 70 + menu.items.length * 40);\n  ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7'; ctx.font = 'bold 22px system-ui';\n  ctx.fillText('Settings', W / 2, 186);\n  ctx.font = '18px system-ui';\n  menu.items.forEach((item, i) => {\n    ctx.fillStyle = i === menu.at ? '#ffd34d' : '#f3eef7';\n    ctx.fillText(`${i === menu.at ? '▸ ' : ''}${item.label()}`, W / 2, 226 + i * 40);\n  });\n}\n\nconnect();\nrequestAnimationFrame(frame);\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '310,430p' vendor/hub/lib/hub/README.md && sed -n '1,200p' vendor/hub/scripts/hub-check.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '310,430p' vendor/hub/lib/hub/README.md && sed -n '1,200p' vendor/hub/scripts/hub-check.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"\nEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\none, the game is not affected.\n\n---\n\n## Test it\n\nThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\nand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\nto the game:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\nThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\n`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n\nThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\n`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\n`\"true\"` at the end. It checks:\n\n- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\n- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\n- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n  player of its own;\n- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n  told the round ended;\n- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\n\n**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\ncases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\n`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\ngame is served from the harness's own origin.\n\nIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\nchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\nruns there.\n\n---\n\n## Reference\n\n### Tags\n\n| Tag | |\n|---|---|\n| `hub:session` | `1`: this protocol |\n| `hub:session-players` | `MIN-MAX`: the number of players the game takes in a session |\n| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\n| `hub:session-goal` | how to win, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-howto` | the controls, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-minutes` | optional: how many minutes a round takes |\n| `hub:webgpu` | optional: `required` when the game cannot run without WebGPU |\n\n### API\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `AIHub.active` | `true` in a session, from the first line |\n| `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card? })` | → `Promise<info \\| null>`; `null`: no hub. `card: true`: the game shows its own card |\n| `AIHub.ready()` | once, when the round can start |\n| `AIHub.answer('ready' \\| 'more')` | on the game's own card, before `start` |\n| `AIHub.time()` | milliseconds since play began: negative in the countdown, `-Infinity` before `start` |\n| `AIHub.on(event, fn)` | returns a function that removes the handler |\n| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\n| `AIHub.result({ time \\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\n| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\n| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\n| `AIHub.rng(label)` | a generator of numbers in `[0, 1)`, the same on every copy, one stream per label |\n| `AIHub.seeded` | `true` when the client seeded `Math.random` |\n| `AIHub.fail(message)` | the game cannot run in this browser |\n\n`AIHub.probe()` and `AIHub.inspect()` exist for older games; the hub does not\nread them.\n\n| Event | Arguments |\n|---|---|\n| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\n| `start` | `{ in }`: milliseconds until play begins |\n| `message` | `data, from` |\n| `leave` | `{ id, reason }` |\n| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\n| `end` | `{ reason, standings }` |\n\nEvents that arrive before a handler is attached are kept, and delivered in\norder when the first handler is attached. Fields and events a newer hub adds\nreach the game through the client unchanged.\n\n### Versions\n\nThis is protocol **1**, client **1.4.0**. Changes within version 1 only add:\ngames on older clients keep working. A change that would break a game becomes\nprotocol 2, with its own `hub:session` value.\n#!/usr/bin/env node\n/**\n * hub-check.mjs — does a game keep the AI Hub Session Protocol?\n *\n * Runs lib/hub/harness.html?auto=1 against each game, at the player counts its\n * hub:session-players allows: hello, ready under the hub's card with no key\n * press, the start, traffic, a player leaving, time-up and a valid result. Then\n * once more with the host leaving. Then the game on its own, outside a session:\n * it opens, Enter and Space are pressed, and it must draw its screen with no\n * errors, the session client inactive and Math.random left alone. Before any\n * game script runs, every frame in session mode gets alert, confirm, prompt,\n * window.open and socket constructors wrapped, so calling them is caught.\n * Needs Playwright, which is not a dependency (see shots.mjs).\n *\n * Parallel is played at 1 and 2 players: nothing is shared, so more copies\n * prove nothing more. Its checks expect Math.random seeded the same on every\n * copy, progress from every copy, and no game traffic.\n *\n * Ghost and shared world are played at 2, 3 and 4 players on a poor network\n * (150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss). Ghost is checked like parallel, except that every\n * copy sends its player. A shared world wants traffic both ways, and is\n * played once more at 2 players with its world hosted by one more copy that\n * has no player of its own, as a dedicated server would host it (README,\n * \"Shared world\"). That run is reported like any; --record does not hold it\n * against a game, since no server runs yet.\n *\n * --retrofit is for an existing game upgraded to parallel: it is played once,\n * at 2 players with one of them leaving. With --original <path>, errors the\n * original page already had are forgiven when it is opened on its own.\n * --draws-only does only that last part, for any page: the retrofit runs it on\n * a game before spending a model on it, since a page this browser cannot run\n * cannot be checked here. A WebGPU-only game without WebGPU is caught even\n * when its title screen shows: it asked for an adapter, got none, and drew\n * nothing with WebGL or a 2D canvas instead. --browser-args passes flags to\n * Chromium; on a machine without a GPU, SwiftShader gives such games a\n * software adapter:\n *   --browser-args \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader\"\n *\n * Every game's pasted client is also read from disk and must be exactly a\n * released one (scripts/lib/hub-client.mjs).\n *\n * --record writes the outcome into data/overrides.json, which is how the hub\n * keeps a failing game out of sessions: a game that fails gets \"session\": \"0\"\n * (it overrides the game's own hub:session meta, so Random Mode never deals\n * it) and a sessionNote naming what failed; a game that passes loses both.\n *\n * Usage:  node scripts/hub-check.mjs [game paths…] [--players 2,3,4] [--base URL] [--json] [--no-solo]\n *                                    [--retrofit [--original <path>]] [--draws-only] [--record] [--browser-args \"<flags>\"]\n *         (games default to the three examples in lib/hub/examples/)\n */\n\nimport { createServer } from 'node:http';\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\nimport { mkdir, readdir, readFile, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n\nimport { staticHandler } from './lib/serve.mjs';\nimport { modeOf, SELF_REPORTED } from '../lib/hub/round.js';\nimport { findClients } from './lib/hub-client.mjs';\n\nconst ROOT = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\nconst EXAMPLES = ['/lib/hub/examples/arena.html', '/lib/hub/examples/ghost.html', '/lib/hub/examples/parallel.html'];\nconst PAGE_MS = 300_000;\n\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst option = (name, fallback) => {\n  const at = args.indexOf(`--${name}`);\n  if (at === -1) return fallback;\n  const [value] = args.splice(at, 2).slice(1);\n  return value;\n};\nconst asked = option('players', null);\nlet base = option('base', null);\nconst original = option('original', null);\nconst asJson = args.includes('--json');\nconst solo = !args.includes('--no-solo');\nconst retrofit = args.includes('--retrofit');\nconst drawsOnly = args.includes('--draws-only');\nconst record = args.includes('--record');\n/** Extra flags for the browser, e.g. the ones that give it WebGPU where the machine can (lib/kit/README.md). */\nconst browserArgs = (option('browser-args', '') || '').split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\nconst asPath = (g) => (g.startsWith('/') || /^https?:/.test(g) ? g : `/${g}`);\nconst games = args.filter((a) => !a.startsWith('--')).map(asPath);\nif (!games.length) games.push(...EXAMPLES);\n\n/**\n * The player counts to try: as asked, or by the game's mode, within the seats\n * the game takes. Parallel shares nothing, so 1 and 2 say it all.\n */\nfunction countsFor(mode, [least, most]) {\n  const list = asked ?? (mode === 'parallel' ? '1,2' : '2,3,4');\n  return list.split(',').map(Number).filter((n) => n >= 1 && n <= 4 && (asked || (n >= least && n <= most)));\n}\n\n/** The game's session mode (older tags read as today's) and its seats, from its head. */\nasync function headOf(game) {\n  try {\n    const html = await (await fetch(/^https?:/.test(game) ? game : `${base}${game}`)).text();\n    const meta = (name) => html.match(new RegExp(`<meta\\\\s+name=[\"']${name}[\"']\\\\s+content=[\"']([^\"']+)[\"']`, 'i'))?.[1] ?? null;\n    const [least = 1, most = least] = (meta('hub:session-players')?.match(/\\d+/g) ?? []).map(Number);\n    return { mode: modeOf(meta('hub:session-mode')), seats: [least, most] };\n  } catch {\n    return { mode: null, seats: [1, 4] };\n  }\n}\n\nlet chromium;\ntry {\n  ({ chromium } = createRequire(import.meta.url)('playwright'));\n} catch {\n  console.error('hub-check needs Playwright: pnpm add -D playwright && pnpm exec playwright install chromium');\n  process.exit(2);\n}\n\n/**\n * Runs in every frame before its own scripts: it notes what the page asks of\n * the graphics stack, and session-mode pages are watched for dialogs and sockets.\n */\nfunction watch() {\n  // What the page asked of the graphics stack: a WebGPU adapter it never got, and\n  // no WebGL drawing instead, means this browser cannot run it (a title screen may still show).\n  const gfx = (window.__gfx = { askedForWebGPU: false, gotAdapter: false, webgl: false, twoD: false });\n  if (navigator.gpu?.requestAdapter) {\n    const ask = navigator.gpu.requestAdapter.bind(navigator.gpu);\n    Object.defineProperty(navigator.gpu, 'requestAdapter', {\n      configurable: true,\n      writable: true,\n      value: async (...a) => {\n        gfx.askedForWebGPU = true;\n        const adapter = await ask(...a);\n        if (adapter) gfx.gotAdapter = true;\n        return adapter;\n      },\n    });\n  }\n  for (const Canvas of [window.HTMLCanvasElement, window.OffscreenCanvas].filter(Boolean)) {\n    const getContext = Canvas.prototype.getContext;\n    Canvas.prototype.getContext = function (type, ...rest) {\n      const context = getContext.call(this, type, ...rest);\n      if (context && /^(webgl2?|experimental-webgl)$/.test(type)) gfx.webgl = true;\n      if (context && type === '2d') gfx.twoD = true;\n      return context;\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (!/[?&]aihub=/.test(location.search)) return;\n  const seen = (window.__hubViolations = []);\n  for (const name of ['alert', 'confirm', 'prompt', 'open']) {\n    window[name] = () => {\n      seen.push(`${name}() called`);\n      return name === 'confirm' ? false : null;\n    };\n  }\n  for (const name of ['WebSocket', 'RTCPeerConnection', 'EventSource']) {\n    const Original = window[name];\n    if (!Original) continue;\n    window[name] = function (...a) {\n      seen.push(`${name} opened in a session (${String(a[0]).slice(0, 80)})`);\n      return new Original(...a);\n    };\n  }\n  addEventListener('error', (e) => seen.push(`error: ${e.message}`));\n  addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (e) => seen.push(`unhandled rejection: ${e.reason?.message || e.reason}`));\n}\n\nlet server = null;\nif (!base) {\n  server = createServer(staticHandler(ROOT));\n  await new Promise((resolve) => server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', resolve));\n  base = `http://127.0.0.1:${server.address().port}`;\n}\n\nconst browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH, args: ['--no-sandbox', '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required', ...browserArgs] });\nconst runs = [];\ntry {\n  for (const game of games) {\n    if (drawsOnly) {\n      const report = await stillWorks(game, null, { bare: true });\n      runs.push({ game, players: 1, scenario: 'draws', pass: report.pass, checks: report.checks });\n      if (!asJson) console.log(`${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}  ${game}  draws on its own`);\n      continue;\n    }\n    const client = await clientCheck(game);\n    if (client) {\n      runs.push({ game, players: 0, scenario: 'static', pass: client.pass, checks: [client] });\n      if (!asJson && !client.pass) console.log(`FAIL  ${game}  ✗ ${client.name} — ${client.detail}`);\n    }\n    const { mode, seats } = await headOf(game);\n    const counts = countsFor(mode, seats);\n    // A retrofit is played once, at 2 players with one leaving: nothing is shared, so that says it all.\n    const plan = retrofit && !asked ? [] : counts.map((n) => ({ n, scenario: 'standard' }));\n    const leaving = retrofit && !asked ? 2 : Math.max(2, Math.min(3, Math.max(...counts, 0)));\n    if (asked || leaving <= seats[1]) plan.push({ n: leaving, scenario: 'host-leave' });\n    // A shared world must also run on a copy with no player of its own, as a server would run it.\n    if (!retrofit && mode && !SELF_REPORTED.includes(mode) && (asked || (seats[0] <= 2 && seats[1] >= 2))) plan.push({ n: 2, scenario: 'server' });\n    for (const { n, scenario } of plan) {\n      const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 860 } });\n      await context.addInitScript(watch);\n      const page = await context.newPage();\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '80,125p' vendor/engine/API.md && cat vendor/engine/docs/ASSETS.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '80,125p' vendor/engine/API.md && cat vendor/engine/docs/ASSETS.md\"","aggregated_output":"- Nothing on screen: the camera looks at the wrong place. Use `game.follow(hero)` once (in the scene's `enter`), or call `game.focus(...)` every update. In side view the hero has y = 0.\n- Walls or level missing: you forgot `map.drawFloor(r)` + `map.queueWalls(r)` (TileMap) or `level.draw(r)` (PlatformMap).\n- Using a TileMap for a side-scroller. Side-scrollers use `E.PlatformMap` + `E.Platformer`.\n- HUD drawn in world coordinates. Use `r.text(...)` or `r.overlay(g => ...)` with screen pixels (`r.W`, `r.H`).\n- An old key layout: platformers want `input: 'PLATFORMER'` (Space jumps), shooters `input: 'SHMUP'` (Space fires).\n- Errors show in a red box on screen and in the console. Fix the first one first.\n- Colours are `'#rrggbb'`, `rgb()`, `hsl()` or a basic name ('orange'); any other draws magenta.\n- `mouseGround()` is `[x, y]`; `settings.reset(group)` resets a group ('Sound'; none: all), not a key; `particles.explosion()` adds a hit-stop and a shake (`{ freeze: false, shake: 0 }`); `E.font.text` outlines unless `outline: false`.\n- A frame past 50 ms gives up its time (no catch-up): a test in a slow browser waits on the game's state, not the clock.\n\n## Game\n`new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', view, views, res, expand, input, bg })`\n- `res`: `'nes'` 256x240, `'snes'` 256x224, `'genesis'` 320x224, `'gb'` 160x144, `'gba'` 240x160, `'ps1'` / `'n64'` 320x240, `'wide'` 400x225, or `[w, h]`. Fixed pixels: whole-number scaling on a desktop screen, the largest fit on a phone (Settings, Pixel scaling). Leave it out for an adaptive size.\n- `expand: true`: full screen at any shape, no bars. `res` becomes the least the screen shows and `r.W` x `r.H` grows to fill the window (a 16:9 monitor shows about 427x240 of `'ps1'`, a phone held upright about 320x690). Anchor the HUD to `r.W` and `r.H`, and give the level something to show in the extra space (more of it, a backdrop, a HUD deck under it on a tall screen). `expand: { maxW, maxH }` caps the growth. A scene may set it too.\n- Adaptive size: `minW` / `minH` set the scale (the screen shows at least that many pixels), `maxW` / `maxH` cap the view (the rest is letterboxed). `portrait: { maxH: 1000 }` overrides them while the screen is taller than wide, so a phone held upright (9:16) is filled instead of showing a band across its middle. `game.screen.portrait` says which way it is.\n- `input`: `'DEFAULT'` (top-down action), `'PLATFORMER'`, `'SHMUP'`, `'THIRDPERSON'`, or your own `{ action: ['KeyQ', 'Pad0'] }`.\n- `views`: the views your game supports; `game.nextView()` cycles them (bind it to a key).\n- Start: `game.start({ update(dt), draw(r) })`, or with scenes (below).\n- Methods: `follow(obj, { z: 16, lead: 20 })` (camera tracks it automatically), `focus(x, y, z)` (or aim it yourself every update), `setView(id)`, `nextView()`, `freeze(s)` (hit-stop: `update` waits; `game.hitstop` is the time left), `shake(n)`, `after(s, fn)`, `every(s, fn)` (timers in game time, return `{ cancel() }`), `hook('input' | 'step' | 'enter', fn)` (your own each step, paused too for input; returns its removal), `mouseGround()`, `go(scene, data)`, `enableGPU({ map })`.\n- Fields: `W`, `H` (screen pixels), `time`, `real`, `timeScale` (0.25 = slow motion), `paused`, `input`, `audio`, `particles`, `lights`, `view`, `errors`, `cam`. `game.fail('my power', err)` reports an error in your code (logged, in `errors`, on the error panel) and plays on.\n- Camera zoom and turn: `game.setZoom(1.5)` (.5 .. 3; everything drawn by the engine re-rasterizes crisply, the HUD stays), `game.rotateView(45)` (ground views only), `game.resetCamera()` (to the scene's zoom), `game.zoom`, `game.yaw`, `game.note('ZOOM 2x')` (a short notice at the top of the screen; `game.shownNote` is the one showing). Custom painters can read `r.view.zoom` (undefined at 1x) to scale their own art.\n- The player's zoom: a scene's `camera: { zoom: [.75, 2], start: 1, tall: 1.5 }` lets the player zoom within `zoom` from `start` (wheel, `-` `=`, pinch, Settings; `false`: none; `AI_GUIDE.md`, Camera).\n- Tests and tools: `new E.Game({ headless: true })` (the default in Node: no screen, sound or DOM; `draw` is skipped, or with `draw: true` run on a stand-in, its errors in `game.errors`) or `{ loop: false }` runs only by `game.advance(seconds, { draw })` (exact fixed steps at once); `input.tap(action)` presses for one step, `input.hold(action, on)`; `game.debug = { snapshot() {...} }` is your game's handle (`tools/check.mjs` prints it); `game.stop()`, `start()`, `dispose()`.\n- Sessions: `?record=1`, then the pause menu's Save session; `node tools/replay.mjs session.json` replays it exactly, headless (`AI_GUIDE.md`, Sessions).\n- Camera: `cam.offset = [dx, dy]` sits the focus that many screen pixels from the centre (above a phone's touch buttons: `[0, -60]`); `cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v)` keeps it inside the level (in side views a level shorter than the screen sits on the bottom edge; `cam.align = 'center'` to change); `cam.room = [160, 128]` moves screen by screen (Zelda, Metroid) and `cam.moving` is true while it slides; `cam.smooth` = lag in seconds (0: locked to the target); `cam.window = [48, 24]` a dead zone the focus moves in before the camera follows; `cam.snapY = true` follows a followed body's height only when it lands (side-scrollers); `cam.frame([p1, p2], { margin, zoom: [.5, 1] })` keeps them all in view, zooming out as they part (`frame(null)` stops); `cam.free = { keys, edge: 10, drag, speed: 300, bounds: [x0, y0, x1, y1] }` a free camera (strategy, sims): keys, a stick, the screen's edge or a drag pan it, a zoom goes toward the pointer or the pinch.\n\n## Scenes (title, play, game over)\n```js\ngame.start({ scene: 'title', scenes: {\n  title: { update(dt) { if (game.input.pressed('start')) game.go('play', { level: 1 }); },\n           draw(r) { r.sky(['#101848', '#402a70']); r.text('PRESS START', r.W / 2, 100, '#fff', { align: 'center', scale: 2 }); } },\n  play: { pausable: true, view: 'side', input: 'PLATFORMER', res: 'snes', views: ['side', 'brawler'], touch: ['jump', 'attack'],\n          enter(data) { /* build the level */ }, exit() {}, update(dt) {}, draw(r) {} }\n} });\n```\n`game.go(name, data)` switches after a short dithered fade (`game.fadeTime`: a test advances past it; `{ fade: 0 }` cuts; `{ fade: 'wipe' | 'iris' | 'mosaic' | 'swirl' | 'dissolve' | 'white', seconds: .4, at: hero }` a transition, a plain fade under reduce motion); timers (but `after(s, fn, { keep: true })`) and particles are cleared, a hit-stop ends (`timeScale` stays). `pausable: true`: Escape / P / Start pauses it, with the pause menu (below). `view`, `views`, `input`, `res`, `expand`, `touch`, `camera`, `propSize` are options applied on entry (a method so named warns). A scene is one object every visit: reset its state in `enter`. `back()` takes a phone's back gesture first (true if it went back: a sub-menu closed).\n\n## Motion and timing: tweens, scripts, paths, weather\n- Tweens (Phaser's): `game.tween(door, { y: 40 }, .5, { ease: 'outBack', delay, repeat, yoyo, onDone, keep })` eases numbers on game time: paused with the game, slowed by `timeScale`, ended by a scene change unless `keep`. Returns `{ done, cancel() }`. `E.ease` has Penner's set: `linear`, `inSine` `outSine` `inOutSine`, `inQuad` `outQuad` `inOutQuad`, the same for `Cubic`, `Back`, `Elastic`, `Bounce`.\n- Scripts (Unity's coroutines) for cutscenes, boss patterns, wave timelines, tutorials:\n```js full-script\ngame.script(function* () {\n  yield 1;                                   // seconds of game time\n  yield E.until(() => door.open);            // a condition\n  yield game.tween(boss, { y: 80 }, 1.5);    // a tween (or another script, or a generator) finishing\n  for (let w = 0; w < 3; w++) { spawnWave(w); yield E.any([8, () => enemies.length === 0]); }\n# Objects and materials as data\n\nThe full engine draws still objects (barrels, tables, trees, wells) from a few lines of data, in every view and facing,\nwith the house shading and outline, and gives every surface (floors, wall faces, wall tops, platform tiles, the objects'\nown faces) a material from one open registry. An object costs one to a few hundred tokens of data (the core's median is\n125); you check it headless with one command. Read this card whole before you write one. (The agent edition keeps the\nregistries and ignores the calls: `E.addAssets` returns empty lists, the others null.)\n\n## Use one\n\n```js\n// in draw(r): feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor; its front toward facing\nr.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing: Math.PI / 2 });\n// once, before the updates: bodies stop at it, a body coming down lands on it, one wholly below passes under\nmap.solid('table', 120, 80, 0, { facing: 0 });\n// a sprite of it, for an inventory or a HUD (r.sprite, px.sprite)\nconst icon = E.shapeSprite('chest', { view: 'iso' });\n```\n\n- **r.shape options:** facing (radians, where the front points: 0 east, π/2 south, as written), scale, mats ({ slot:\n  material }), flip (mirrors it x to -x, collision too), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (default true),\n  light (adds its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true).\n- **map.solid** takes the same id and placement, so one object can feed both calls. Bodies span z to z + h (E.Body's h, 32).\n- **In 3D** the 3D engine draws the same entries, materials and boxes: `world.shape(id, x, y, z, o)` (its header).\n- **Steep views** (top-down) draw shapes from the characters' lower angle, as rigs are drawn. The light comes from the\n  viewer's upper left in every view.\n- **Glow and fire:** a material with glow: 1 ignores the light and stays bright in the dark; an entry's flames ([[x, y, z,\n  w, h]]) draw the engine's animated flame (r.shape only: a sprite has none). Anything else that moves stays a prop\n  (r.prop) or your own code.\n- **Dressing a generated level:** a scene is a few entries as [id, across, forward] from an anchor (a wall spot, forward\n  into the room); place it whole or not at all, each part on free floor, after the level's own random picks and from a\n  seeded stream of its own, so the level stays as its seed builds it (Emberdeep's `src/emberdeep/53-scenes.js`).\n\n## The core library\n\n**Shapes** (sized for a 26-unit hero; generators take params): barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed,\nbookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, well, sign, lamppost, anvil; fence { len: 16 }, pine { h: 41, tiers: 4 },\ntree { h: 40, seed: 1 }, bush { r: 7 }, grass { h: 6, n: 6 }, rock { r: 7.5, seed: 2 }, crystal { h: 18, seed: 1 }.\n`r.shape('pine', x, y, 0, { params: { h: 30 } })`; `E.SHAPES.barrel.about` says what each is.\n\n**Materials:** woods oak walnut birch crate plank planks wood; stones stone cobble marble granite sandstone slate rock\nbrick flagstone ruin; metals iron steel gold copper bronze metal rusted; clay glazed porcelain; cloth linen burlap wool velvet leather;\nplants bark needles leaves shrub moss straw hedge grass; ground dirt sand snow mud; water ice crystal flame bone shingle;\nwalls timber plaster; tops speckle plain tiles slab; tiles block bonus ground pipe checker.\n\n## Materials on surfaces\n\n```js\nE.MATERIALS.mossy = { color: '#6a7a5a', pattern: 'stones', size: 6 };   // or the shorthand '#6a7a5a stones size=6'\nconst types = { 1: { h: 32, top: '#6a6280', side: '#4a4360', face: 'cobble', roof: 'slate' } };   // TileMap walls\nconst map = new E.TileMap({ rows, legend, types, floorMat: 'flagstone', floorMats: { water: 'water' } });   // floors\nconst level = new E.PlatformMap({ rows, legend, types: { 1: { kind: 'solid', style: 'block', mat: 'mossy' } } });\n```\n\nfloorMats is keyed by the floor tags of the legend ('~': { floor: 'water' }); either stands in for floorTex.\n\nA material is `{ color, pattern, ...the pattern's numbers, ramp, glow, over }`. Its five tones come from `E.tones(color)`\n(or its own `ramp` of five, dark to light); the light picks a band, the pattern moves it a step, so a material works on\nevery surface and in every palette and recolors with one hex. An unknown name warns with the list of names.\nOverlays, the last on top, each in its own color's tones: `over: [['moss', '#5f7a3a', { up: .6 }], ['cracks']]`; moss on\nwhat looks up, cracks (the material a step darker), dirt near the ground (h 6), rust; each takes amount and size.\n\n| Pattern | Numbers | What |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| none | | the light alone |\n| planks | bw 3, len 14, dir | boards with joints; staves on round parts; dir: 'v' turns them |\n| crate | frame 2, bw 3 | a framed, braced side; planks on its lid |\n| bricks | bw 6, bh 3, mortar | running bond |\n| stones | size 5 | irregular stones (Voronoi), dark joints, a lit rim |\n| tiles | size 4 | square tiles, grout |\n| speck, noise | amount .08; scale 4 | specks; soft patches |\n| foliage | size 3.5 | leaf clumps lit on top |\n| bark | | fissures; rings on a cut end |\n| metal | rivet | a shine where lit; rivets |\n| cloth | fold .9 | weave and folds |\n| glaze | | a glossy shine |\n| thatch, shingles | course; bw | straw courses; roof tiles |\n\nYour own pattern: `E.PATTERNS.waves = (s, m) => Math.sin(s.u / (m.size || 3)) > .8 ? 1 : 0` (s.u, s.v: world units\nacross and up the surface; s.lid, s.curved, s.lit, s.W, s.H; return a step, -1 to +2). A material may also paint one kind\nof surface its own way, per pixel: `face(wx, z, tones, type, cx, cy, fi, nh, h)` or `roof(wx, wy, tones, type)` returning\na color or null, `floor(x, y, tag, view)` returning [r, g, b].\n\n## Write one\n\nUnits: 16 = 1 m = one tile; x east, y south, z up. The origin is the middle of the footprint on the ground; write it\nfacing south (+y). Use whole or half units: a pixel at game size is about 0.7 units.\n\n```js\nE.SHAPES.stool = { about: 'round three-legged stool', tags: 'furniture tavern', mats: { w: 'oak', l: 'walnut' },\n  parts: [['cyl','w',[0,0,8],5,1.5], ['ring',3,3,['box','l',[0,0,0],[1.5,1.5,8],{rot:[0,-8,0]}]]] };\n```\n\nAn entry: `about`, `tags`, `mats` (slot to material; a slot name that is not in mats is a material itself), and `parts`, or\n`make(params)` returning parts with `params` its defaults. Optional: `scale` (times the placement's), `foot: [x0, y0,\nx1, y1]` (the footprint for collision, and for sorting when it stands raised; the bounds by default), `lights: [[x, y,\nz, color, radius]]`, `flames: [[x, y, z, w, h]]`.\n\n| Part | Form | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| box | `['box', m, at, [w, d, h], { rot }]` | at: the bottom middle |\n| cyl | `['cyl', m, at, r, h, { r2, seg, sq }]` | r2: top radius (0: a cone); sq squashes y; seg: 6 for a hexagon |\n| lathe | `['lathe', m, at, [[r, z], ...], { seg }]` | a profile turned about z, bottom to top; [0, z] closes an end |\n| ball | `['ball', m, at, r, { sz }]` | at: its centre; sz below 1 flattens it |\n| prism | `['prism', m, at, [[a, b], ...], h, { axis }]` | an outline pushed h: up z (outline x, y), or centred along y (outline x, z) or x (outline y, z) |\n| wedge | `['wedge', m, at, [w, d, h]]` | h tall at the back, down to the floor at the front |\n| rock | `['rock', m, at, r, { sz, seed, rough }]` | a lumpy, faceted ball; below the floor is not drawn |\n| use | `['use', id, at, { rot, scale, mats, ...params }]` | another shape inside this one |\n| mirror | `['mirror', 'x' \\| 'y' \\| 'xy', part]` | the part and its mirror copies |\n| ring, row | `['ring', n, radius, part]`, `['row', n, [dx, dy, dz], part]` | n copies round z (the part moved out to radius); n copies in a line, centred |\n| group | `['group', at, rot, [parts]]` | parts moved and turned together |\n\nEvery part takes `{ rot }`: a yaw in degrees, or [x, y, z] degrees. Write arrays densely (`[0,0,8]`, not `[0, 0, 8]`):\nspaces cost a third more tokens.\n\n### Worked entries\n\n```js\nbarrel: { about: 'oak barrel, two iron hoops', tags: 'container wood', mats: { w: 'oak', h: 'iron' },\n  parts: [['lathe','w',[0,0,0],[[0,0],[5,0],[6,3],[6.5,8],[6,13],[5,16],[0,16]]], ['row',2,[0,0,9],['cyl','h',[0,0,7.5],6.5,1.5]]] },\ncrate: { about: 'wooden crate, framed and braced', tags: 'container wood', mats: { c: 'crate' }, parts: [['box','c',[0,0,0],[15,15,14]]] },\ntable: { about: 'plank table, four legs', tags: 'furniture tavern', mats: { t: 'oak', l: 'walnut' },\n  parts: [['box','t',[0,0,10],[24,14,2]], ['mirror','xy',['box','l',[10,5,0],[2,2,10]]]] },\nchest: { about: 'oak chest, round lid, iron bands', tags: 'container treasure', mats: { w: 'oak', b: 'iron', l: 'gold' },\n  parts: [['box','w',[0,0,0],[16,10,8]], ['prism','w',[0,0,8],[[-5,0],[5,0],[4,3],[0,5],[-4,3]],16,{axis:'x'}],\n    ['mirror','x',['box','b',[5.5,0,0],[1.5,11,8.5]]], ['box','l',[0,5,5],[3,1,3]]] },\nlamppost: { about: 'iron street lamp, glowing head', tags: 'town light', mats: { m: 'iron', g: 'flame' }, lights: [[0,0,40,'#ffd070',70]],\n  parts: [['cyl','m',[0,0,0],2.5,3], ['cyl','m',[0,0,3],1,34], ['box','g',[0,0,37],[4,4,5]], ['cyl','m',[0,0,42],3.5,3,{r2:0,seg:4}]] },\nfence: { about: 'rail fence, len long (16)', tags: 'village farm', mats: { w: 'oak' }, params: { len: 16 },\n  make: p => [['mirror','x',['box','w',[p.len / 2 - 1,0,0],[2,2,12]]], ['row',2,[0,0,5],['box','w',[0,0,6],[p.len - 2,1,1.5]]]] },\n```\n\nA generator seeds its noise from its params (`E.rng(seed)`), never `Math.random`, so it draws the same pixels everywhere.\n\n## Make one: the recipe\n\n1. **Read this card whole.**\n2. **Find** the nearest entry: `node tools/asset-find.mjs \"tavern table\"` searches the core library and the store's sets\n   (`src/assets/sets/`, about a thousand objects, materials and sprites converted from CC0 libraries, each with where it\n   came from) and `--show set:id` prints one; the Asset Lab (`/asset-lab`) shows them all.\n3. **Copy** it and change its names, parts and materials, or write a new one from the parts above. Give the cue a player\n   knows it by parts of its own (a skep's coils as stacked rings, an anvil's horn, a barrow's open tub dark inside), and\n   keep small parts plain ('none', 'glaze'): a busy pattern on a part a few pixels wide reads as speckle.\n4. **Look:** `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#stool` (a file that sets `E.SHAPES.stool`, or a store set; a core id\n   alone works too: `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs barrel`). It draws `check-output/asset-sheet/stool.png`: every view and\n   four facings, beside the hero, on a light and a dark floor. It lints what reads badly: too small from above, a part\n   under a pixel, too few tones, low contrast with the floor, its tokens. Read the picture, fix, repeat.\n5. **Use** it: `E.SHAPES.stool = {...}` and `r.shape('stool', ...)`; or a set file\n   (`(window.ASSETS = window.ASSETS || {}).MINE = { set: 'MINE', format: 1, materials, shapes }`) and\n   `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS.MINE)`, which names its entries 'MINE:stool' so they never collide, and returns the names.\n   A store set loads the same way (its script, then `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`);\n   `node tools/asset-set.mjs <sets> --ids a,b --name mine --out mine.js` cuts the few a game uses, with what they need\n   (Emberdeep's set dressing loads `src/assets/sets/emberdeep.js`, cut so).\n\n## Limits\n\n- Still objects. Lids that open, swinging signs and held weapons are code (or props) for now.\n- A shape sorts by one point, as props do; a long one (a bed, a cart) may cross a body walking right beside it.\n- Collision is the footprint's box, turned with the shape, and the bounds' height: a table is solid under its top too.\n- Bigger than about 240 pixels on screen, a shape skips the actors' effects (flash, x-ray).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
