{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > docs/issues.md <<'EOF'\n# Unique issue ledger\n\nOnly observed implementation defects are counted. Duplicate failing cases count once. A test-script import-name collision and a CSS pseudo-element changing an accessible selector were fixed in test tooling and do not count as game defects.\n\n| ID | Severity | Detection | Fix / state |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| SF-01 | Major | First 1/2-pilot full bot trace missed anchor introduction: scout died before release. | Added an explicit charging anchor to the authored escort encounter. Verified in full 1–4-pilot simulations. |\n| SF-02 | Medium | First full-play trace finished in 549 active seconds and screenshot showed long cleared pockets. | Added deliberate reinforcement groups and boss pacing; final successful runs target 10–12 active minutes. |\n| SF-03 | Medium | 1920×1080 title screenshot showed native Shell flex alignment placing menu over upper-right art. | Game stylesheet now sets title flex direction explicitly; title-menu bounding-box check covers placement. |\n| SF-04 | Major | Full-run checks for boost/pulse-only upgrade choices lost the base during the longer boss fight. | Reduced incidental ground-projectile chip damage; bomber impacts, lane volleys and landed divers remain consequential. All upgrade branches now win without cheats. |\n| SF-05 | Minor | Swept-hit and gravity tests could not construct a telegraph-free charged anchor because kind defaults overwrote spawn options. | Anchor/relay defaults now respect explicit scenario options. Swept collision and boost escape checks pass. |\n| SF-06 | Minor | Heat-overflow restoration test cooled a boundary value below 100 before resolution. | Cooling is disabled at overflow, preserving the retreat outcome. |\n\n## Implementation review corrections (not testing issue counts)\n\n- Pointer aim now follows the native aim source while movement keys are held, rather than following only the last prompt device.\n- Couch join callback preserves native half-keyboard maps.\n- A completed reliable keyframe is applied to recover entities even when more recent small updates have already arrived, then the latest small update is reapplied.\n- Boss batteries now mark the actual locked impact lane before releasing their volley.\nEOF\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Checkpoint — bundled playable siege\n- All game modules exist: src/data, src/sim, src/render, audio.js, input.js, ui/screens.js, online.js, main.js and style.css.\n- Reproducible \"'`npm run build` emits root final HTML plus development game.html; no runtime dependencies. Exact released Hub client comes first after charset; full native engine is included unchanged once.\n- Root exit-interview.json exists and drives in-game About via the bundler; testing feedback is still unknown until final checks.\n- `node tools/verify.mjs simulation` now passes 23 meaningful checks, including all 3 upgrade paths and 1/2/4-player no-cheat full victories, forced retreats/defeat, deterministic snapshots, collision/resource/priority checks and native draw independence.\n- Six unique game issues recorded in docs/issues.md; none currently classified critical/game-breaking. Browser/Hub checks may add findings.\n- Browser suite is active (exec session 97160) and uses actual root artifact. It will emit only failures via verifier. Next run Hub suite and implement any fixes. Inspect evidence screenshots, finish controls/docs/feedback, then final complete verifier.\n- Official harness support copied unchanged into tests/hub. Scoped server is owned by Python test and bound 127.0.0.1 port 0.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > docs/issues.md <<'EOF'\n# Unique issue ledger\n\nOnly observed implementation defects are counted. Duplicate failing cases count once. A test-script import-name collision and a CSS pseudo-element changing an accessible selector were fixed in test tooling and do not count as game defects.\n\n| ID | Severity | Detection | Fix / state |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| SF-01 | Major | First 1/2-pilot full bot trace missed anchor introduction: scout died before release. | Added an explicit charging anchor to the authored escort encounter. Verified in full 1–4-pilot simulations. |\n| SF-02 | Medium | First full-play trace finished in 549 active seconds and screenshot showed long cleared pockets. | Added deliberate reinforcement groups and boss pacing; final successful runs target 10–12 active minutes. |\n| SF-03 | Medium | 1920×1080 title screenshot showed native Shell flex alignment placing menu over upper-right art. | Game stylesheet now sets title flex direction explicitly; title-menu bounding-box check covers placement. |\n| SF-04 | Major | Full-run checks for boost/pulse-only upgrade choices lost the base during the longer boss fight. | Reduced incidental ground-projectile chip damage; bomber impacts, lane volleys and landed divers remain consequential. All upgrade branches now win without cheats. |\n| SF-05 | Minor | Swept-hit and gravity tests could not construct a telegraph-free charged anchor because kind defaults overwrote spawn options. | Anchor/relay defaults now respect explicit scenario options. Swept collision and boost escape checks pass. |\n| SF-06 | Minor | Heat-overflow restoration test cooled a boundary value below 100 before resolution. | Cooling is disabled at overflow, preserving the retreat outcome. |\n\n## Implementation review corrections (not testing issue counts)\n\n- Pointer aim now follows the native aim source while movement keys are held, rather than following only the last prompt device.\n- Couch join callback preserves native half-keyboard maps.\n- A completed reliable keyframe is applied to recover entities even when more recent small updates have already arrived, then the latest small update is reapplied.\n- Boss batteries now mark the actual locked impact lane before releasing their volley.\nEOF\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Checkpoint — bundled playable siege\n- All game modules exist: src/data, src/sim, src/render, audio.js, input.js, ui/screens.js, online.js, main.js and style.css.\n- Reproducible \"'`npm run build` emits root final HTML plus development game.html; no runtime dependencies. Exact released Hub client comes first after charset; full native engine is included unchanged once.\n- Root exit-interview.json exists and drives in-game About via the bundler; testing feedback is still unknown until final checks.\n- `node tools/verify.mjs simulation` now passes 23 meaningful checks, including all 3 upgrade paths and 1/2/4-player no-cheat full victories, forced retreats/defeat, deterministic snapshots, collision/resource/priority checks and native draw independence.\n- Six unique game issues recorded in docs/issues.md; none currently classified critical/game-breaking. Browser/Hub checks may add findings.\n- Browser suite is active (exec session 97160) and uses actual root artifact. It will emit only failures via verifier. Next run Hub suite and implement any fixes. Inspect evidence screenshots, finish controls/docs/feedback, then final complete verifier.\n- Official harness support copied unchanged into tests/hub. Scoped server is owned by Python test and bound 127.0.0.1 port 0.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
