{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_83","type":"agent_message","text":"The official Hub harness passes for 1–4 players, dedicated hosting, and host departure with 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter, and 5% loss. Browser checks also found a recursive credits Back action that caused a runtime error. I’m fixing that and adding deeper checks for snapshot recovery, host clock catch-up, and natural victory reporting.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_84","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('src/ui/screens.js');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"  class SiegeShell extends My3D2dge.Shell{\\\\n\\\", \\\"  class SiegeShell extends My3D2dge.Shell{\\\\n    back(){if(this.screen==='title')return this;return super.back();}\\\\n    _step(){const root=this.screen==='title';super._step();if(root&&\"'!this.screen&&this.app?.mode==='\"'title')this.app.ui.title();}\\\\n\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"title,sections:slice,actions:acts,back:()=>this.shell.back()\\\", \\\"title,sections:slice,actions:acts\\\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat >> docs/issues.md <<'EOF'\n| SF-09 | Critical | Full credits navigation raised an uncaught “Maximum call stack size exceeded” and could not return to the index. | Removed a custom Back callback that recursively called the native Back handler. Native stack navigation now owns the return; root-title cancel is also guarded. |\n| SF-10 | Medium | Portrait screenshot made the canvas HUD too small to read even though the full arena fitted. | Added a portrait-only native Shell objective/score/hull HUD in the unused letterbox area and moved compact radio captions clear of it. |\nEOF\nnpm run build\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_84","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('src/ui/screens.js');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"  class SiegeShell extends My3D2dge.Shell{\\\\n\\\", \\\"  class SiegeShell extends My3D2dge.Shell{\\\\n    back(){if(this.screen==='title')return this;return super.back();}\\\\n    _step(){const root=this.screen==='title';super._step();if(root&&\"'!this.screen&&this.app?.mode==='\"'title')this.app.ui.title();}\\\\n\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"title,sections:slice,actions:acts,back:()=>this.shell.back()\\\", \\\"title,sections:slice,actions:acts\\\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat >> docs/issues.md <<'EOF'\n| SF-09 | Critical | Full credits navigation raised an uncaught “Maximum call stack size exceeded” and could not return to the index. | Removed a custom Back callback that recursively called the native Back handler. Native stack navigation now owns the return; root-title cancel is also guarded. |\n| SF-10 | Medium | Portrait screenshot made the canvas HUD too small to read even though the full arena fitted. | Added a portrait-only native Shell objective/score/hull HUD in the unused letterbox area and moved compact radio captions clear of it. |\nEOF\nnpm run build\"","aggregated_output":"npm notice run space-fortnight@1.0.0 build\nnpm notice run node tools/build.mjs --quiet\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_85","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '41,78p' tests/hub/harness.html && sed -n '345,379p' tests/hub/harness.html && sed -n '540,575p' tests/hub/harness.html && sed -n '2899,2932p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_85","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '41,78p' tests/hub/harness.html && sed -n '345,379p' tests/hub/harness.html && sed -n '540,575p' tests/hub/harness.html && sed -n '2899,2932p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js\"","aggregated_output":"</head>\n<body>\n<header>\n  <h1>AI Hub session harness</h1>\n  <label>Game <input class=\"game\" id=\"game\" placeholder=\"mygame.html or /games/mygame/index.html\"></label>\n  <label>Players <select id=\"players\"><option>1</option><option selected>2</option><option>3</option><option>4</option></select></label>\n  <label>Latency <input type=\"number\" id=\"latency\" min=\"0\" value=\"60\"> ms</label>\n  <label>Jitter <input type=\"number\" id=\"jitter\" min=\"0\" value=\"20\"> ms</label>\n  <label>Loss <input type=\"number\" id=\"loss\" min=\"0\" max=\"50\" value=\"0\"> %</label>\n  <button id=\"restart\" type=\"button\">New round</button>\n  <button id=\"release\" type=\"button\" title=\"End the splash now: the round starts once every game has loaded\">Start now</button>\n  <button id=\"timeup\" type=\"button\">Time up</button>\n  <label>Remove <select id=\"who\"></select></label>\n  <button id=\"remove\" type=\"button\">Remove player</button>\n  <button id=\"hide\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Hide host tab</button>\n</header>\n<main>\n  <div id=\"grid\"><p class=\"hint\" style=\"padding:16px\">Name a game above (a path or URL served alongside this page), then press New round. Click a player's frame to control that player.</p></div>\n  <aside>\n    <section><h2>Round</h2><div id=\"round\" class=\"hint\">No round yet.</div></section>\n    <section id=\"checks\"><h2>Conformance</h2><ul id=\"checklist\"><li class=\"hint\">Run with <code>?auto=1</code> for the automatic checks.</li></ul></section>\n    <pre id=\"log\" aria-live=\"off\"></pre>\n  </aside>\n</main>\n<script type=\"module\">\nimport { createBridge, attachFrame, postTo, createLocalNetwork } from './bridge.js';\nimport { createRound, limitFor, modeOf, seedsRandom, SELF_REPORTED, TIMINGS } from './round.js';\n\nconst NAMES = ['Red Fox', 'Blue Otter', 'Green Heron', 'Gold Lynx'];\nconst params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\nconst $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);\nconst auto = params.get('auto') === '1';\nconst scenario = params.get('scenario') || 'standard';\n/** ?scenario=server: the shared world runs on one more copy with no player of its own, as a dedicated server would run it. */\nconst serverMode = scenario === 'server';\nconst playMs = Number(params.get('play')) || 6000;\nconst SPLASH_MS = 10_000;\n\n    bits.push(`↑${cell.bridge.stats.sent} ↓${cell.bridge.stats.received}`);\n    cell.label.querySelector('.cell__state').textContent = bits.join(' · ');\n    cell.el.classList.toggle('is-out', !!p.out || cell.gone);\n  }\n  const lines = [`Round ${s.round} · ${s.mode || 'mode unknown'} · phase ${s.phase}`, `Host: ${s.server ? 'the server, no player' : `player ${s.host}`} · seed ${state.seed}`];\n  if (s.gate && !s.released) lines.push(`Card: ${state.cells.some((c) => c.bridge.showsCard) ? 'the game’s own, ' : ''}${state.splashUntil ? `${Math.max(0, Math.ceil((state.splashUntil - performance.now()) / 1000))} s left` : 'held'} (Start now ends it)`);\n  if (state.record) {\n    const name = (id) => s.players[id]?.name ?? `#${id}`;\n    lines.push(`Ended ${state.record.status} (${state.record.reason})`);\n    if (state.record.standings) state.record.standings.forEach((ids, i) => lines.push(`  ${i + 1}. ${ids.map(name).join(', ')}`));\n  }\n  if (s.issues.length) lines.push(...s.issues.map((i) => `✗ ${i.key}: ${i.problem}`));\n  $('round').textContent = lines.join('\\n');\n}\n\n$('restart').onclick = () => newRound();\n$('release').onclick = () => releaseRound();\n$('timeup').onclick = () => current?.coordinator.timeUp();\n$('remove').onclick = () => {\n  const cell = current?.cells.find((c) => c.key === $('who').value);\n  if (cell) removeCell(cell);\n};\n$('hide').onclick = () => {\n  if (!current) return;\n  current.hidden = !current.hidden;\n  $('hide').setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(current.hidden));\n  (current.cells.find((c) => c.server) ?? current.cells[0])?.bridge.visibility(current.hidden);\n  log(`host tab ${current.hidden ? 'hidden' : 'shown'}`);\n};\nfor (const id of ['latency', 'jitter', 'loss']) $(id).onchange = applyNet;\n\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n * ?auto=1 — the conformance run. It presses keys inside each frame with\n * synthetic events while the round plays (the frames must be served from this\n * page's origin). Results land in window.__hubCheck, and body[data-complete]\n    }),\n  );\n}\n\nif (auto) conformance();\nelse if ($('game').value) newRound();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n  _enter(name, data) {\n    const s = this.scenes[name];\n    if (!s) throw new Error('scene \"' + name + '\" does not exist. Scenes: ' + Object.keys(this.scenes).join(', '));\n    const old = this.scene;\n    if (old && old.exit) old.exit();\n    if (old && old._propWas !== undefined) { E.style.propSize = old._propWas; old._propWas = undefined; }\n    this.scene = s; this.sceneName = name; this.paused = false; if (old) prune(this._timers, t => !t.keep); this.hitstop = 0;   // (timers made before the first scene live into it)\n    this.particles.list.length = 0; this.cam.snap = true; this.audio._duck(false); this._follow = this._framed = null;\n    const ok = sceneField(name, s);\n    if (ok('view')) this.setView(s.view);\n    if (ok('views')) this.views = s.views;\n    if (ok('input')) this.input.use(s.input);\n    if (ok('res') || ok('expand')) this.screen.setOptions(Object.assign(ok('res') ? { res: s.res } : {}, ok('expand') ? { expand: s.expand } : {}));\n    if (ok('touch')) this.input.touchButtons(s.touch);\n    ok('camera');\n    if (s.propSize !== undefined) { s._propWas = E.style.propSize; E.style.propSize = s.propSize; }   // scene option: prop scale while this scene runs\n    this._zoomFit(true);   // its camera: its zoom to start at, and whether the player's applies\n    if (s.pausable || name === 'main') this._fsAuto = this._autoFull();   // a game starting from a tap goes full screen again\n    for (const f of HOOKS.enter) f(this, old);\n    this._ownRun('enter', name, data);\n    if (s.enter) s.enter(data);\n  }\n  /** report an error in game code without stopping the game: logged once per place and message, kept in game.errors\n   *  and shown on the error panel (the engine reports its own callbacks' errors this way): game.fail('power ' + id, err) */\n  fail(where, e) {\n    const msg = (e && e.message) || String(e), key = where + ':' + msg;\n    if (!this._errKeys.has(key)) {\n      this._errKeys.add(key); this.errors.push({ where, scene: this.sceneName, message: msg, stack: e && e.stack });\n      console.error('my-3D2dge: error in ' + where + (this.sceneName ? ' (scene \"' + this.sceneName + '\")' : '') + ': ' + ((e && e.stack) || msg));\n    }\n    E.showError('error in ' + where + '()' + (this.sceneName && this.sceneName !== 'main' ? ' of scene \"' + this.sceneName + '\"' : ''), e);\n    if (this.onError) try { this.onError(e, where); } catch (e2) { /* ignore */ }\n  }\n  _step(dt) {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_86","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('tests/browser_checks.py');s=p.read_text();needle='    finally:\\\\n        browser.close();server.shutdown();server.server_close();thread.join(timeout=2)'\ninsert='''        # Stateful gameplay checks use the same official bridge/round in manual mode.\n        ctx=browser.new_context(viewport={'width':1400,'height':960});page=ctx.new_page();page.set_default_timeout(6000)\n        def remote_gameplay():\n            page.goto(base+'/tests/hub/harness.html?game=/game.html&players=2&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=0')\n            page.wait_for_function('[...document.querySelectorAll(\\\"iframe\\\")].length===2 && [...document.querySelectorAll(\\\"iframe\\\")].every(f=>f.contentWindow.__fortnight?.online)')\n            frames=[f for f in page.frames if f\"'!=page.main_frame];host,remote=frames\n            remote.evaluate('\"'__game.input.hold(\\\"right\\\");__game.input.hold(\\\"fire\\\")')\n            page.wait_for_timeout(150)\n            need(host.evaluate('__fortnight.world.s.tick')==0,'Unreleased Hub mutated')\n            page.locator('#release').click()\n            page.wait_for_timeout(250)\n            need(host.evaluate('__fortnight.world.s.tick')==0,'Countdown mutated')\n            host.wait_for_function('__fortnight.world.s.phase===\\\"play\\\"',timeout=12000)\n            page.wait_for_timeout(350)\n            moved=host.evaluate('__fortnight.world.s.players.find(p=>p.id===1).x')\n            need(moved>500,'Real remote intent did not move host ship')\n            need(host.evaluate('__fortnight.world.s.events.some(e=>e.type===\\\"shot\\\"&&e.owner===1)'),'Remote fire never became an authoritative shot')\n            remote.evaluate('__game.input.hold(\\\"right\\\",false);__game.input.hold(\\\"fire\\\",false)')\n            invalid=host.evaluate('''\\\"\\\"\\\"()=>{const o=__fortnight.online,w=__fortnight.world,p=w.s.players[1],seq=p.seq,e=w.s.epoch;\n              o.receive({t:'i',e,v:{...Fortnight.neutral(seq+1),mx:NaN}},1);\n              o.receive({t:'i',e,v:{...Fortnight.neutral(seq+1),mx:1,my:1}},1);\n              o.receive({t:'i',e,v:Fortnight.neutral(seq)},1);\n              o.receive({t:'i',e,v:Fortnight.neutral(seq+99)},99);\n              return p.seq===seq;}\\\"\\\"\\\"''')\n            need(invalid,'Invalid identity/vector/sequence was accepted')\n            host.evaluate('__game.menu()');tick=host.evaluate('__fortnight.world.s.tick');page.wait_for_timeout(150)\n            need(host.evaluate('__game.paused') and host.evaluate('__fortnight.world.s.tick')>tick+8,'Host local menu froze shared world')\n            need(host.locator('.esh-btns').get_by_text('Return to command',exact=True).count()==0,'Hub offered invalid navigation')\n            host.evaluate('__fortnight.ui.shell.hide()')\n            host.evaluate('clearInterval(__fortnight.timer)');tick=host.evaluate('__fortnight.world.s.tick');page.wait_for_timeout(500)\n            need(host.evaluate('__fortnight.world.s.tick')==tick,'RAF also advanced the authority')\n            host.evaluate('__fortnight.timer=setInterval(()=>__game.advance(.016,{draw:false}),16)');page.wait_for_timeout(150)\n            lag=host.evaluate('Math.floor(AIHub.time()/1000/Fortnight.DT)-__fortnight.world.s.tick')\n            need(abs(lag)<8,'Authority did not catch up after timer delay: '+str(lag))\n            host.evaluate('''\\\"\\\"\\\"()=>{const w=__fortnight.world;w.jump(1,2);w.s.base=77;w.s.heat=50;for(const p of w.s.players){p.inv=0;w.damagePlayer(p);}__fortnight.online.lastFull=-10;}\\\"\\\"\\\"''')\n            page.wait_for_timeout(2300)\n            remote.wait_for_function('__fortnight.world.s.act===1 && __fortnight.online.lastKeyTick>0')\n            h=host.evaluate('({phase:__fortnight.world.s.phase,act:__fortnight.world.s.act,score:__fortnight.world.s.score,base:__fortnight.world.s.base,hp:__fortnight.world.s.players.map(p=>p.hp)})')\n            r=remote.evaluate('({phase:__fortnight.world.s.phase,act:__fortnight.world.s.act,score:__fortnight.world.s.score,base:__fortnight.world.s.base,hp:__fortnight.world.s.players.map(p=>p.hp)})')\n            need(h==r,'Recoverable full state did not converge: '+str([h,r]))\n            host.evaluate('window.finishCalls=0;window.realFinish=AIHub.finish;AIHub.finish=(r)=>{finishCalls++;window.finishPayload=r;return realFinish(r)}')\n            page.locator('#timeup').click();page.locator('#timeup').click()\n            host.wait_for_function('__fortnight.online.ended')\n            need(host.evaluate('finishCalls')==1,'Time-up finished more than once')\n            need(host.evaluate('finishPayload.standings.length===1&&finishPayload.standings[0].length===2&&Number.isFinite(finishPayload.scores[0])'),'Invalid co-op result')\n            return {'host':h,'remote':r,'clockLagTicks':lag}\n        check('Hub remote fire/control, inert countdown, malicious/stale input, local overlay, timer catch-up and complete snapshot convergence',remote_gameplay)\n        ctx.close()\n        ctx=browser.new_context(viewport={'width':1400,'height':960});page=ctx.new_page();page.set_default_timeout(6000)\n        def dedicated_victory():\n            page.goto(base+'/tests/hub/harness.html?game=/game.html&players=2&scenario=server&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=0')\n            page.wait_for_function('document.querySelectorAll(\\\"iframe\\\").length===3 && [...document.querySelectorAll(\\\"iframe\\\")].every(f=>f.contentWindow.__fortnight?.online)')\n            frames=[f for f in page.frames if f\"'!=page.main_frame]\n            host=next(f for f in frames if f.evaluate('\"'__fortnight.online.info.server'))\n            need(host.evaluate('__game.headless && \"'!__fortnight.painter && __game.audio.ctx===null'\"'),'Dedicated host created local rendering/audio')\n            page.locator('#release').click();host.wait_for_function('AIHub.time()>=0',timeout=10000)\n            value=host.evaluate('''\\\"\\\"\\\"()=>{window.finishCalls=0;window.realFinish=AIHub.finish;AIHub.finish=r=>{finishCalls++;window.finishPayload=r;return realFinish(r)};\n              const w=__fortnight.world;let peak=0;\n              for(let i=0;i<100000&&\"'!w.s.result;i++){for(const p of w.s.players){w.setIntent(p.id,Fortnight.botIntent(w,p.id,p.seq+1));if(w.s.phase==='\"'upgrade')w.upgrade(p.id,p.id%3);}w.step();\n                if(i%120===0)peak=Math.max(peak,Fortnight.encodeWorld(w.s).length);}\n              return {result:w.s.result,seen:w.s.seen,phases:w.s.bossPhases,active:w.s.activeTime,limit:AIHub.limitMs/1000,peak};} \\\"\\\"\\\"''')\n            need(value['result']['won'] and len(value['seen'])==8 and value['phases']==[0,1,2],'Dedicated full siege did not naturally win')\n            need(590<value['active']<value['limit'] and value['peak']<=48000,'Siege exceeds round or snapshot capacity')\n            host.wait_for_function('__fortnight.online.ended',timeout=10000)\n            page.wait_for_timeout(250)\n            need(host.evaluate('finishCalls')==1,'Natural victory finished more than once')\n            need(host.evaluate('finishPayload.won===true&&finishPayload.standings[0].length===2'),'Natural result invalid')\n            for f in frames:\n                need(f.evaluate('__fortnight.world.s.result?.won===true'),'Final victory was not delivered to a client')\n                need(f.evaluate('__fortnight.world.s.score')==value['result']['score'],'Final score differs across copies')\n                need(not f.evaluate('__game.errors'),'Natural full run raised engine error')\n            (ROOT/'evidence/hub-dedicated-victory.json').write_text(json.dumps(value,indent=2))\n            return value\n        check('dedicated host full no-cheat siege, every mechanic, bounded snapshots, real victory and exactly one tied finish',dedicated_victory)\n        ctx.close()\n'''\nif needle not in s:raise Exception('marker not found')\ns=s.replace(needle,insert+needle);p.write_text(s)\nPY\npython3 -m py_compile tests/browser_checks.py\nnode tools/verify.mjs hub\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
