{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_123","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'docking|enterAct|montage|startSolo' tools/capture_motion.py && cat docs/issues.md\"","aggregated_output":"32:            \"docking\",\n45:        if name == \"docking\":\n46:            page.evaluate('__fortnight.world.enterAct(2);__fortnight.ui.lastPhase=\"\"')\n49:                \"__fortnight.startSolo();__game.advance(.01);__game.debug.advance(750,{bot:true,draw:false})\"\n60:                \"montage\",\n# Unique issue ledger\n\nOnly observed implementation defects are counted. Duplicate failing cases count once. A test-script import-name collision and a CSS pseudo-element changing an accessible selector were fixed in test tooling and do not count as game defects.\n\n| ID | Severity | Detection | Fix / state |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| SF-01 | Major | First 1/2-pilot full bot trace missed anchor introduction: scout died before release. | Added an explicit charging anchor to the authored escort encounter. Verified in full 1–4-pilot simulations. |\n| SF-02 | Medium | First full-play trace finished in 549 active seconds and screenshot showed long cleared pockets. | Added deliberate reinforcement groups and boss pacing; final successful runs target 10–12 active minutes. |\n| SF-03 | Medium | 1920×1080 title screenshot showed native Shell flex alignment placing menu over upper-right art. | Game stylesheet now sets title flex direction explicitly; title-menu bounding-box check covers placement. |\n| SF-04 | Major | Full-run checks for boost/pulse-only upgrade choices lost the base during the longer boss fight. | Reduced incidental ground-projectile chip damage; bomber impacts, lane volleys and landed divers remain consequential. All upgrade branches now win without cheats. |\n| SF-05 | Minor | Swept-hit and gravity tests could not construct a telegraph-free charged anchor because kind defaults overwrote spawn options. | Anchor/relay defaults now respect explicit scenario options. Swept collision and boost escape checks pass. |\n| SF-06 | Minor | Heat-overflow restoration test cooled a boundary value below 100 before resolution. | Cooling is disabled at overflow, preserving the retreat outcome. |\n\n## Implementation review corrections (not testing issue counts)\n\n- Pointer aim now follows the native aim source while movement keys are held, rather than following only the last prompt device.\n- Couch join callback preserves native half-keyboard maps.\n- A completed reliable keyframe is applied to recover entities even when more recent small updates have already arrived, then the latest small update is reapplied.\n- Boss batteries now mark the actual locked impact lane before releasing their volley.\n| SF-07 | Major | Real browser's very short right-click landed and released between fixed updates, so held-only action sampling missed pulse. | Intent adapter now combines native pressed and down for fire, boost and pulse. |\n| SF-08 | Medium | Phone contact test placed a thumb in the lower letterbox and the adapter discarded it. | Invisible floating controls now accept the entire canvas; right-thumb drags supply a direction, including portrait letterbox space. |\n\nBrowser test maintenance: native Back icon and Back action have the same accessible name, so checks scope action selectors to the native action group. Pad press timing was changed to accommodate headless rendering cadence; that is not counted as a game defect.\n| SF-09 | Critical | Full credits navigation raised an uncaught “Maximum call stack size exceeded” and could not return to the index. | Removed a custom Back callback that recursively called the native Back handler. Native stack navigation now owns the return; root-title cancel is also guarded. |\n| SF-10 | Medium | Portrait screenshot made the canvas HUD too small to read even though the full arena fitted. | Added a portrait-only native Shell objective/score/hull HUD in the unused letterbox area and moved compact radio captions clear of it. |\n| SF-11 | Medium | Boss screenshot showed the tutorial panel covering the newly docked player. | Moved desktop guidance to a compact side panel clear of the initial wing positions and shortened its display. Portrait uses separate letterbox space. |\n| SF-12 | Medium | Results screenshot clipped the second navigation action at the initial scroll position. | Reduced results spacing and put both actions on one row at TV sizes, retaining controller scrolling on smaller screens. |\n| SF-13 | Major | Touch attract-exit regression found a generated click could activate a newly revealed title button. | Added a short click-capture quarantine matching the existing input consumption window. Keyboard, pointer, pad and touch exits are checked. |\n\nAdditional implementation review fixes, excluded from the testing issue count: per-pad meaningful-activity states now reset on release; held meaningful sticks prevent idle; menu gestures update native prompt device; entry selection checks every co-op pilot; fortress anchors are kept clear of the opaque armor. The new safe-entry regression also checks those invariants.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_124","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nroot=Path('..');p=root/'exit-interview.json';data=json.loads(p.read_text())\ndata['sourceInformation']['animation']='Native E.anim sprite frames/rotation, native easing and tween-driven victory flyout, plus simulation-driven recoil, shields, gravity, radiator cooling, sliding boss shutters, docking and retreat.'\ndata['sourceInformation']['testing']='Unrestricted headless testing with no FPS target. 51 checks: fixed-step simulation, Chromium/Firefox/WebKit, synthetic standard pads, phone/tablet touch, offline Web Audio and the official adverse-network Hub harness. Physical controllers, actual iOS, public internet hosting and human listening quality: unknown.'\ndata['sourceInformation']['research']='Visually inspected the Century flyer and six sampled gameplay frames; read the Museum of the Game entry, MAME CVS driver, engine handoff/API/ROCKS kit and current Hub client/README/example/harness/checker. Original music and exact scoring: unknown. Full links and revisions in development docs/research.md.'\ndata['testingFeedback']=[\n'13 unique game defects found and fixed; test-tool errors and review-only corrections are excluded. The verifier passes 51 checks.',\n'1 critical runtime issue: a recursive credits Back callback. It is fixed and navigation is covered by the browser suite.',\n'The no-cheat full siege across every upgrade branch. It exposed ground-base damage that made the longer non-laser boss fights lose.',\n'The initial title-only smoke check. It helped composition but said little about combat, progression or multiplayer.'\n]\ndata['engineFeedback']=[\n'The native pixel shading, sprite animation, procedural audio buses and controller-navigable Shell fit this arcade game well.',\n'I gave a Shell Back callback another call to Back, causing recursion. A real credits-navigation test found it; native stack navigation fixed it.',\n'A deterministic three-act siege simulation, authored director and authoritative co-op replication with recoverable bounded snapshots.',\n'Coordinating the fixed arena, portrait HUD and a host clock that keeps running while a local menu or hidden-tab timer interrupts rendering.',\n'None to the released engine. It is bundled unchanged; game-specific Shell subclasses, input adapters and scheduling use its public systems.',\n'Include a tested shared-world authority clock and compact snapshot example in the handoff.'\n]\ndata['promptFeedback']=[\n'The complete vertical-slice goal, source research and concrete single-file hand-in contract.',\n'Space Fortress names several unrelated games; PLAN.md resolves the interpretation to Century Electronics / CVS.',\n'Making three connected defensive acts, every upgrade branch, controller/touch UX and authoritative co-op obey one state model.',\n'Include the pinned engine and Hub handoffs with the task, and distinguish required acceptance gates from optional examples.'\n]\nassert set(data)=={'sourceInformation','testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback','aiHub'}\nassert [len(data[k]) for k in ['testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback']]==[4,6,4]\np.write_text(json.dumps(data,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nq=Path('src/ui/screens.js');s=q.read_text().replace('const size = kind === \\\"source\\\" ? 4 : 2,','const size = 2,');q.write_text(s)\nq=Path('src/style.css');s=q.read_text()+'''\\\\n.esh .esh-sh[aria-label=\\\"Source Information\\\"] .esh-btns,\n.esh .esh-sh[aria-label\"'$=\"Feedback\"] .esh-btns{flex-direction:row;flex-wrap:wrap}\n.esh .esh-sh[aria-label=\"Source Information\"] .esh-btns button,\n.esh .esh-sh[aria-label$=\"Feedback\"] .esh-btns button{flex:1;min-width:120px;text-align:center}\n'\"''';q.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/issues.md');s=p.read_text();rows=[line for line in s.splitlines() if line.startswith('| SF-')]\nassert len(rows)==13\np.write_text('''# Unique issue ledger\n\n13 unique game defects found and fixed, including one critical runtime error. Duplicate failures count once. Test-tool faults and review-only corrections are excluded.\n\n| ID | Severity | Detection | Fix / state |\n|---|---|---|---|\n'''+ '\\\\n'.join(rows)+'''\n\n## Implementation review corrections (excluded from defect counts)\n\n- Pointer aim follows the native aim source while movement keys are held.\n- Couch joining preserves native half-keyboard maps.\n- Complete reliable keyframes recover entities even when newer small updates have arrived; the latest small update is reapplied afterward.\n- Boss batteries mark their actual locked impact lane before release. Compact boss clocks/health keep client shutters and weak points current.\n- Per-pad meaningful activity resets after release, held meaningful input prevents idle, and menu gestures select the native prompt device.\n- Entry placement checks every co-op pilot; fortress anchors remain clear of opaque armor.\n\n## Test-tool corrections (excluded from defect counts)\n\n- Renamed an inspection helper that shadowed Python's inspect module.\n- Scoped native action selectors to distinguish the Back icon from the Back action and accounted for a title button's CSS arrow in its accessible name.\n- Pad automation waits for actual native poll/release state rather than assuming a browser frame rate.\n- Departing Hub iframes are detached by the official harness; checks inspect remaining frames.\n- Wrapped a finish-counter installation in an explicit function so Playwright would not invoke the newly assigned callback as its return value.\n- Explicit font path is used for ImageMagick filmstrip assembly.\n''')\np=Path('tools/capture_motion.py');s=p.read_text().replace('__fortnight.world.enterAct(2);','__fortnight.world.s.boss=null;__fortnight.world.enterAct(2);');p.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat > docs/testing.md <<'EOF'\n# Verification evidence\n\nRun \"'`npm run verify` from the development folder. It captures child chatter, prints failures if present and one final count. The final full run covers 51 functional checks; reports are saved in evidence/{simulation,browser,hub}-checks.json. Build the artifact with `npm run build`.\n\n- **25 simulation checks:** seeded full wins without cheats at 1, 2 and 4 pilots, all upgrade branches, all eight threats, all three boss phases, 10–12-minute active pacing, forced retreats and final defeat, deterministic replay/recovery, empty boost, cooling, tractor/pulse/gravity escape, pickup/kill idempotence, invulnerability, swept hit/miss, team redeploy/wipe priority, validated data-only added encounter, safe entry placement and native-render independence.\n- **18 browser checks:** actual delivered file:// artifact and exact client placement; real keyboard/mouse movement, aiming, short clicks and resize; pause/dev sliders/reset/single-step/preview; settings persistence/rebinding; factual paged credits; full win and real defeat/retries; ten-second attract, complete tour and input-class exits; native art in every act; offline audio and bus cleanup; four synthetic controllers and reserved chord; two keyboard halves; phone/tablet multitouch/cancellation/rotation; denied storage; WebKit phone and Firefox Canvas 2D smoke.\n- **8 Hub checks:** six unchanged official conformance runs at 1/2/3/4 players plus dedicated server and host departure; then deeper remote-control/fire, inert countdown, malicious/stale input, neutral local overlay, delayed timer catch-up, recoverable state convergence, once-only time-up and dedicated-host full victory checks. Network is the official local bridge with 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss.\n\nThe dedicated no-cheat victory record is evidence/hub-dedicated-victory.json. It demonstrates approximately 610 active seconds within the actual 900-second harness ceiling, every mandatory introduction, all boss phases and a genuine tied team win. Peak compact complete state measured in that authored run was under 8 KB; it is split into reliable chunks. Every routine packet is asserted at or below 1200 bytes, every packet below 16 KB, and combined sends are capped at 18 per second. Game traffic and sound stop after end.\n\nOffline audio evidence is evidence/audio-signals.json: finite, non-silent music/SFX/gibberish, with bounded peaks. Music defaults to 0.1 and saved choices persist. These are signal checks, not listening.\n\nPurposeful screenshots cover title, all defensive acts, gravity, boss, victory/defeat, credits, controller tuning and phone/tablet framing. Native animation filmstrips cover pulse/boost, boss shutters, ground docking and victory flyout. See tools/capture_motion.py for the deterministic engine-clock capture.\n\nLimitations: pads and touch are synthetic; WebKit profiles are desktop emulation, not actual iOS; no physical TV, controller, phone or tablet was used. Public internet deployment and human audio quality are unknown. No FPS benchmark or optimization target was introduced. All test servers are owned, bound to 127.0.0.1 on an OS-selected port, identified before use and shut down by their creating process.\n\nThe issue ledger records 13 unique corrected game defects, one critical. Engine source and the released Hub client are unchanged. In-game metadata and root exit-interview.json share the same source through the bundler.\nEOF\nbiome check --write --linter-enabled=false --assist-enabled=false src tools/*.mjs tests/simulation.mjs package.json\nruff check tests/browser_checks.py tools/*.py\nruff format tools/capture_motion.py\nnpm run build\nnpm run verify'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
