ledger\n\n13 unique game defects found and fixed, including one critical runtime error. Duplicate failures count once. Test-tool faults and review-only corrections are excluded.\n\n| ID | Severity | Detection | Fix / state |\n|---|---|---|---|\n'''+ '\\\\n'.join(rows)+'''\n\n## Implementation review corrections (excluded from defect counts)\n\n- Pointer aim follows the native aim source while movement keys are held.\n- Couch joining preserves native half-keyboard maps.\n- Complete reliable keyframes recover entities even when newer small updates have arrived; the latest small update is reapplied afterward.\n- Boss batteries mark their actual locked impact lane before release. Compact boss clocks/health keep client shutters and weak points current.\n- Per-pad meaningful activity resets after release, held meaningful input prevents idle, and menu gestures select the native prompt device.\n- Entry placement checks every co-op pilot; fortress anchors remain clear of opaque armor.\n\n## Test-tool corrections (excluded from defect counts)\n\n- Renamed an inspection helper that shadowed Python's inspect module.\n- Scoped native action selectors to distinguish the Back icon from the Back action and accounted for a title button's CSS arrow in its accessible name.\n- Pad automation waits for actual native poll/release state rather than assuming a browser frame rate.\n- Departing Hub iframes are detached by the official harness; checks inspect remaining frames.\n- Wrapped a finish-counter installation in an explicit function so Playwright would not invoke the newly assigned callback as its return value.\n- Explicit font path is used for ImageMagick filmstrip assembly.\n''')\np=Path('tools/capture_motion.py');s=p.read_text().replace('__fortnight.world.enterAct(2);','__fortnight.world.s.boss=null;__fortnight.world.enterAct(2);');p.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat > docs/testing.md <<'EOF'\n# Verification evidence\n\nRun \"'`npm run verify` from the development folder. It captures child chatter, prints failures if present and one final count. The final full run covers 51 functional checks; reports are saved in evidence/{simulation,browser,hub}-checks.json. Build the artifact with `npm run build`.\n\n- **25 simulation checks:** seeded full wins without cheats at 1, 2 and 4 pilots, all upgrade branches, all eight threats, all three boss phases, 10–12-minute active pacing, forced retreats and final defeat, deterministic replay/recovery, empty boost, cooling, tractor/pulse/gravity escape, pickup/kill idempotence, invulnerability, swept hit/miss, team redeploy/wipe priority, validated data-only added encounter, safe entry placement and native-render independence.\n- **18 browser checks:** actual delivered file:// artifact and exact client placement; real keyboard/mouse movement, aiming, short clicks and resize; pause/dev sliders/reset/single-step/preview; settings persistence/rebinding; factual paged credits; full win and real defeat/retries; ten-second attract, complete tour and input-class exits; native art in every act; offline audio and bus cleanup; four synthetic controllers and reserved chord; two keyboard halves; phone/tablet multitouch/cancellation/rotation; denied storage; WebKit phone and Firefox Canvas 2D smoke.\n- **8 Hub checks:** six unchanged official conformance runs at 1/2/3/4 players plus dedicated server and host departure; then deeper remote-control/fire, inert countdown, malicious/stale input, neutral local overlay, delayed timer catch-up, recoverable state convergence, once-only time-up and dedicated-host full victory checks. Network is the official local bridge with 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss.\n\nThe dedicated no-cheat victory record is evidence/hub-dedicated-victory.json. It demonstrates approximately 610 active seconds within the actual 900-second harness ceiling, every mandatory introduction, all boss phases and a genuine tied team win. Peak compact complete state measured in that authored run was under 8 KB; it is split into reliable chunks. Every routine packet is asserted at or below 1200 bytes, every packet below 16 KB, and combined sends are capped at 18 per second. Game traffic and sound stop after end.\n\nOffline audio evidence is evidence/audio-signals.json: finite, non-silent music/SFX/gibberish, with bounded peaks. Music defaults to 0.1 and saved choices persist. These are signal checks, not listening.\n\nPurposeful screenshots cover title, all defensive acts, gravity, boss, victory/defeat, credits, controller tuning and phone/tablet framing. Native animation filmstrips cover pulse/boost, boss shutters, ground docking and victory flyout. See tools/capture_motion.py for the deterministic engine-clock capture.\n\nLimitations: pads and touch are synthetic; WebKit profiles are desktop emulation, not actual iOS; no physical TV, controller, phone or tablet was used. Public internet deployment and human audio quality are unknown. No FPS benchmark or optimization target was introduced. All test servers are owned, bound to 127.0.0.1 on an OS-selected port, identified before use and shut down by their creating process.\n\nThe issue ledger records 13 unique corrected game defects, one critical. Engine source and the released Hub client are unchanged. In-game metadata and root exit-interview.json share the same source through the bundler.\nEOF\nbiome check --write --linter-enabled=false --assist-enabled=false src tools/*.mjs tests/simulation.mjs package.json\nruff check tests/browser_checks.py tools/*.py\nruff format tools/capture_motion.py\nnpm run build\nnpm run verify'","aggregated_output":"Checked 17 files in 17ms. Fixed 1 file.\nAll checks passed!\n1 file reformatted\n51 checks passed; 0 failed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
